window.KB_BODY[55]={"3377903":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Metric Thread Insert Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for repairing damaged metric threads using metric thread insert kit, Part Number 3822709. The kit is used with alignment fixture, Part Number ST 1232.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800537.png\" alt=\"22800537.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Metric Thread Insert Kit, Part Number 3822709</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822698</td><td>Insert, M6 x 1.0 (1 shown)</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822699</td><td>Insert, M8 x 1.25 (1 shown)</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822700</td><td>Insert, M10 x 1.5 (1 shown)</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822701</td><td>Insert, M12 x 1.25 (1 shown)</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822702</td><td>Insert, M12 x 1.5 (1 shown)</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822703</td><td>Insert, M12 x 1.75 (1 shown)</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822704</td><td>Insert, M14 x 2.0 (1 shown)</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822705</td><td>Insert, M16 x 1.5 (1 shown)</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822706</td><td>Insert, M16 x 2.0 (1 shown)</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3824038</td><td>Thread-locking compound</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3824715</td><td>Primer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163757</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3377556</td><td>Kit content bulletin</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with Metric Thread Insert Kit, Part Number 3822709, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>ST 1232</td><td>Drill/ream fixture</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164019</td><td>Chip vacuum</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>See Table 3</td><td>Drill bushing</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800538.png\" alt=\"22800538.png\"></figure><p>Insert</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Thread Insert Dimensions</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Number</td><td>Internal Thread Size (1)</td><td>External Thread Size (2)</td><td>Drill Size</td><td>Overall Length (3)</td><td>Drill Bushing</td></tr><tr><td>3822698</td><td>M6 x 1.0</td><td>3/8-16</td><td>5/16 (0.3125)</td><td>3/4-in</td><td>4918170</td></tr><tr><td>3822699</td><td>M8 x 1.25</td><td>1/2-13</td><td>27/64 (0.421)</td><td>15/16-in</td><td>4918172</td></tr><tr><td>3822700</td><td>M10 x 1.5</td><td>9/16-12</td><td>31/64 (0.484)</td><td>1-1/8-in</td><td>3376495</td></tr><tr><td>3822701</td><td>M12 x 1.25</td><td>5/8-18</td><td>37/64 (0.578)</td><td>1-3/8-in</td><td>ST-1234</td></tr><tr><td>3822702</td><td>M12 x 1.5</td><td>5/8-18</td><td>37/64 (0.578)</td><td>1-3/8-in</td><td>ST-1234</td></tr><tr><td>3822703</td><td>M12 x 1.75</td><td>5/8-18</td><td>37/64 (0.578)</td><td>1-3/8-in</td><td>ST-1234</td></tr><tr><td>3822704</td><td>M14 x 2.0</td><td>3/4-16</td><td>11/16 (0.687)</td><td>1-1/8-in</td><td>ST-1236</td></tr><tr><td>3822705</td><td>M16 x 1.5</td><td>7/8-14</td><td>13/16 (0.812)</td><td>1-1/4-in</td><td>4918173</td></tr><tr><td>3822706</td><td>M16 x 2.0</td><td>7/8-14</td><td>13/16 (0.812)</td><td>1-1/4-in</td><td>4918173</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Install the correct spacers and washers onto the fixture alignment capscrews.</p><p>Install the capscrew and spacer assemblies through the mounting slot of the fixture.</p><p>Finger-tighten the fixture mounting capscrew.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800539.png\" alt=\"22800539.png\"></figure><p>Use a tapered pin to align the guide bar and bushing over the damaged capscrew thread.</p><p>Push downward on the tapered pin and tighten the fixture mounting capscrew.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>67 n•m [49 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800540.png\" alt=\"22800540.png\"></figure><p>Using the information in Table 3, obtain the correct drill size.</p><p>Install the appropriate-size drill/ream bushing.</p><p>If necessary, mark the drill with tape for the required drill depth before starting the drilling operation.</p><p>Drill to the bottom of the original capscrew hole.</p><p>Remove the alignment fixture.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800541.png\" alt=\"22800541.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips from the newly drilled capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Stop frequently to clean the bore using a chip vacuum.</p></div></div><p>Using the information contained in Table 3, External Thread Size, obtain correct tap size.</p><p>Tap the full depth of the hole using a suitable tapping fluid.</p><p>Remove the tap.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800542.png\" alt=\"22800542.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips from the newly tapped capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><p>Thread the appropriate tap in and out of the newly cut threads several times to verify the thread condition, and clean debris from the threads.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800542.png\" alt=\"22800542.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some solvents are flammable and toxic. Read the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions before using.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Check the capscrew hole for evidence of porosity and cracks.</p></div></div><p>Clean the threads, and flush any debris from the tapped hole using a solvent-degreasing agent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00068.png\" alt=\"22a00068.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips and solvent-degreasing agent from the newly tapped capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><p>Place the appropriate jam nut (1) on a capscrew.</p><p>Install the appropriate thread salvage insert (2) onto the capscrew until the capscrew nears the bottom of the insert. Rotate the jam nut (1) until it contacts the thread salvage insert (2).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00070.png\" alt=\"22a00070.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some solvents are flammable and toxic. Read the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions before using.</p></div></div><p>Remove the preservative coating from the circumference of the thread salvage insert using a solvent-degreasing agent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00079.png\" alt=\"22a00079.png\"></figure><p>Apply a light coat of Primer to the thread insert and the threaded hole; allow 3 to 5 minutes to dry.</p><p>Apply four beads of thread-locking compound, Part Number 3824038, to the circumference of the thread salvage insert. Each bead <b>must</b> be 0.8 mm [0.03 in] wide down the entire length of the thread salvage insert, and the beads <b>must</b> be 90 degrees apart.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00073.png\" alt=\"22a00073.png\"></figure><p>Install the insert until it is flush with the block or it bottoms in the hole.</p><p>Allow to dry for 3 hours.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800543.png\" alt=\"22800543.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Remove the capscrew and jam nut.</p><p>If necessary, file or machine the top of the thread salvage insert so that it is flush with the surface.</p><p>Make certain that the inner diameter of the thread salvage insert is free of burrs. Remove any file shavings or debris with the chip vacuum.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00074.png\" alt=\"22a00074.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>It is important that sufficient thread engagement be maintained after this repair.</p></div></div><p>Install a replacement capscrew until it bottoms out in the repaired hole.</p><p>Measure the distance from under the capscrew head to the component&#x27;s surface. Make certain that this dimension is a minimum of 2 mm [0.079 in] less than the thickness of the component and gasket to be attached.</p><p>If the distance is within tolerance, the installation is complete. If the distance is <b>not</b> within tolerance, the capscrew can be shortened slightly, or a shorter capscrew can be used. If a shorter capscrew is used, make certain that a minimum thread engagement of 1-1/2 times the capscrew diameter is maintained.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>22800544.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/22/8/22800544.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div>","3377905":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Thread Insert Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for repairing damaged threads using thread insert kit, Part Number 3376448. The kit is used with alignment fixture, Part Number ST 1232.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800537.png\" alt=\"22800537.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Thread Insert Kit, Part Number 3376448</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376447</td><td>Insert, 9/16-18 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376437</td><td>Insert, 1/4-20 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376438</td><td>Insert, 5/16-18 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376439</td><td>Insert, 3/8-16 (1 shown)</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376440</td><td>Insert, 3/8-24 (1 shown)</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376441</td><td>Insert, 7/16-14 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376442</td><td>Insert, 7/16-20 (1 shown)</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376443</td><td>Insert, 1/2-13 (1 shown)</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376444</td><td>Insert, 5/8-11 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376445</td><td>Insert, 5/8-18 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376446</td><td>Insert, 1/2-20 (1 shown)</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3824038</td><td>Thread-locking compound</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3824715</td><td>Primer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163757</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3822708</td><td>Kit content bulletin</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with Thread Insert Kit, Part Number 3376448, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>ST 1232</td><td>Drill/ream fixture</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164019</td><td>Chip vacuum</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>See Table 3</td><td>Drill bushing</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800538.png\" alt=\"22800538.png\"></figure><p>Insert</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Thread Insert Dimensions</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Number</td><td>Internal Thread Size (1)</td><td>External Thread Size (2)</td><td>Drill Size</td><td>Overall Length (3)</td><td>Drill Bushing</td></tr><tr><td>3376347</td><td>9/16-18</td><td>11/16-16</td><td>33/64 (0.609)</td><td>1.18-in</td><td>ST-1234</td></tr><tr><td>3376437</td><td>1/4-20</td><td>3/8-16</td><td>5/16 (0.312)</td><td>0.75-in</td><td>4918170</td></tr><tr><td>3376438</td><td>5/16-18</td><td>7/16-14</td><td>U (0.368)</td><td>0.93-in</td><td>4918171</td></tr><tr><td>3376439</td><td>3/8-16</td><td>1/2-13</td><td>27/64 (0.421)</td><td>1.13-in</td><td>4918172</td></tr><tr><td>3376440</td><td>3/8-24</td><td>1/2-13</td><td>27/64 (0.421)</td><td>1.07-in</td><td>4918172</td></tr><tr><td>3376441</td><td>7/16-14</td><td>9/16-12</td><td>31/64 (0.484)</td><td>1.15-in</td><td>3376495</td></tr><tr><td>3376442</td><td>7/16-20</td><td>9/16-12</td><td>31/64 (0.484)</td><td>1.21-in</td><td>3376495</td></tr><tr><td>3376443</td><td>1/2-13</td><td>5/8-11</td><td>17/32 (0.531)</td><td>1.51-in</td><td>3376495</td></tr><tr><td>3376444</td><td>5/8-11</td><td>13/16-16</td><td>3/4 (0.750)</td><td>1.64-in</td><td>ST-1237</td></tr><tr><td>3376445</td><td>5/8-18</td><td>13/16-16</td><td>3/4 (0.750)</td><td>1.36-in</td><td>ST-1237</td></tr><tr><td>3376446</td><td>1/2-20</td><td>5/8-11</td><td>17/32 (0.531)</td><td>1.19-in</td><td>3376495</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Install the correct spacers and washers onto the fixture alignment capscrews.</p><p>Install the capscrew and spacer assemblies through the mounting slot of the fixture.</p><p>Finger-tighten the fixture mounting capscrew.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800539.png\" alt=\"22800539.png\"></figure><p>Use a tapered pin to align the guide bar and bushing over the damaged capscrew thread.</p><p>Push downward on the tapered pin and tighten the fixture mounting capscrew.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>67 n•m [49 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800540.png\" alt=\"22800540.png\"></figure><p>Using the information in Table 3, obtain the correct drill size.</p><p>Install the appropriate size drill/ream bushing.</p><p>If necessary, mark the drill with tape for the required drill depth before starting the drilling operation.</p><p>Drill to the bottom of the original capscrew hole.</p><p>Remove the alignment fixture.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800541.png\" alt=\"22800541.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips from the newly drilled capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Stop frequently to clean the bore using a chip vacuum.</p></div></div><p>Using the information contained in Table 3, External Thread Size, obtain correct tap size.</p><p>Tap the full depth of the hole using a suitable tapping fluid.</p><p>Remove the tap.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800542.png\" alt=\"22800542.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips from the newly tapped capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><p>Thread the appropriate tap in and out of the newly cut threads several times to verify the thread condition, and clean debris from the threads.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800542.png\" alt=\"22800542.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some solvents are flammable and toxic. Read the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions before using.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Check the capscrew hole for evidence of porosity and cracks.</p></div></div><p>Clean the threads, and flush any debris from the tapped hole using a solvent-degreasing agent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00068.png\" alt=\"22a00068.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use the chip vacuum attached to compressed air to remove the chips and solvent-degreasing agent from the newly tapped capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00063.png\" alt=\"22a00063.png\"></figure><p>Place the appropriate jam nut (1) on a capscrew.</p><p>Install the appropriate thread salvage insert (2) onto the capscrew until the capscrew nears the bottom of the insert. Rotate the jam nut (1) until it contacts the thread salvage insert (2).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00070.png\" alt=\"22a00070.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some solvents are flammable and toxic. Read the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions before using.</p></div></div><p>Remove the preservative coating from the circumference of the thread salvage insert using a solvent-degreasing agent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00079.png\" alt=\"22a00079.png\"></figure><p>Apply a light coat of Primer to the thread insert and the threaded hole; allow 3 to 5 minutes to dry.</p><p>Apply four beads of thread-locking compound, Part Number 3824038, to the circumference of the thread salvage insert. Each bead <b>must</b> be 0.8 mm [0.03 in] wide down the entire length of the thread salvage insert, and the beads <b>must</b> be 90 degrees apart.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00073.png\" alt=\"22a00073.png\"></figure><p>Install the insert until it is flush with the block or it bottoms in the hole.</p><p>Allow to dry for 3 hours.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800543.png\" alt=\"22800543.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Remove the capscrew and jam nut.</p><p>If necessary, file or machine the top of the thread salvage insert so that it is flush with the surface.</p><p>Make certain that the inner diameter of the thread salvage insert is free of burrs. Remove any file shavings or debris with the chip vacuum.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00074.png\" alt=\"22a00074.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>It is important that sufficient thread engagement be maintained after this repair.</p></div></div><p>Install a replacement capscrew until it bottoms out in the repaired hole.</p><p>Measure the distance from under the capscrew head to the component&#x27;s surface. Make certain that this dimension is a minimum of 2 mm [0.079 in] less than the thickness of the component and gasket to be attached.</p><p>If the distance is within tolerance, the installation is complete. If the distance is <b>not</b> within tolerance, the capscrew can be shortened slightly, or a shorter capscrew can be used. If a shorter capscrew is used, make certain that a minimum thread engagement of 1-1/2 times the capscrew diameter is maintained.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>22800544.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/22/8/22800544.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div>","3377908":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Stem Seal Depth Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>The cylinder head valve stem seal depth gauge, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3164462\">3164462</a>, is used to set the required clearance when installing the valve stem seal for the QSK19, QSK45, and QSK60. This gauge is used with the valve seal installer to set the clearance, which allows the seal to function properly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400109.png\" alt=\"22400109.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Valve Stem Seal Depth Gauge, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3164462\">3164462</a></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3164462\">3164462</a></td><td>Valve stem seal depth gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To avoid the valve seal fitting loosely on the valve guide, do not lubricate the valve seal. The seal must be installed dry.</p></div></div><p>Place the valve stem seal depth gauge over the valve guide and move the smaller slot of the gauge into the valve guide groove area over the shoulder.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400110.png\" alt=\"22400110.png\"></figure><p>Install the valve stem seal on the valve guide until it is positioned against the valve stem seal depth gauge.</p><p>Slide the valve stem seal depth gauge to the large end of the slot and remove the gauge, passing over the valve stem seal outside diameter.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400111.png\" alt=\"22400111.png\"></figure>","3377915":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Compression Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using compression gauge, Part Number 3164627. The gauge is designed for use on diesel engines and has a test range of 0 to 5516 kPa [0 to 800 psi] that is divided into 100 kPa [20 psi] increments. The compression gauge is reset to zero with a push button release valve. The gauge is used to measure cylinder pressure (at cranking speed) on the A1400, A1700, A2000, A2300, A2300T, B3.3, B3.9, QSB3.9-30, QSB4.5-30, B5.9, QSB5.9-30, B4.5 s, B6.7 s and C8.3 series engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00149.png\" alt=\"22d00149.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Compression Gauge, Part Number 3164627</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164627</td><td>Compression gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Compression Gauge, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164839</td><td>B series compression tester (2-valve)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164728</td><td>B3.3 series compression tester</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3164840</td><td>C series compression tester (2-valve)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165128</td><td>A1400, A1700, A2000, A2300, and A2300T compression tester</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Remove all injectors. Refer to the following Troubleshooting and Repair or Master Repair Manuals:</p><ul><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B Series Engines 1991 and 1994 Certification Levels, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666087\">3666087</a></li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B Series Engines, Bulletin 3810207</li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B3.3 Engines, Bulletin 3666418</li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual C Series Engines 1991 and 1994 Certification Levels, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a></li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual C Series Engines, Bulletin 3810261</li><li>Master Repair Manual A Series, Bulletin 4021433.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900073.png\" alt=\"22900073.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that no fuel or oil remain in the combustion chamber after the injectors have been removed. If fuel or oil remain in the cylinder during the compression test, damage to the compression gauge can result.</p></div></div><p>Temporarily disable the fuel injection system.</p><p>Rotate the engine using the starter to remove any remaining fuel or oil from the combustion chamber. Install the appropriate compression tester into the injector bore. For the C Series engine, install the injector clamp and capscrew.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>20 n•m [180 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900074.png\" alt=\"22900074.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Press the release button on the compression gauge to release the pressure before removing the gauge from the engine. Failure to do so can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Connect the compression gauge to the compression tester.</p><p>Refer to the appropriate Troubleshooting and Repair or Master Repair Manual for the compression testing procedure.</p><p>Disconnect the compression gauge from the compression tester. Remove the compression tester. For the C Series engine, remove the capscrew, injector clamp, and compression tester.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900075.png\" alt=\"22900075.png\"></figure><p>Install all injectors. Refer to the following Troubleshooting and Repair or Master Repair Manuals:</p><ul><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B Series Engines 1991 and 1994 Certification Levels, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666087\">3666087</a></li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B Series Engines, Bulletin 3810207</li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual B3.3 Engines, Bulletin 3666418</li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual C Series Engines 1991 and 1994 Certification Levels, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a></li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual C Series Engines, Bulletin 3810261</li><li>Master Repair Manual A Series, Bulletin 4021433.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900073.png\" alt=\"22900073.png\"></figure>","3377920":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Cylinder Head Mounting Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using cylinder head mounting kit, Part Number 3164913. The kit is used to mount the Signature, ISX, ISX with CM870, and QSX15 cylinder head to the engine stand, Part Number 3375194.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00242.png\" alt=\"22c00242.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Cylinder Head Mounting Kit, Part Number 3164913</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164957</td><td>Mounting plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3251767</td><td>Hexagon head capscrew, M10 x 1.5 x 50-mm, class 10.9</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4001226\">4001226</a></td><td>Hexagon head capscrew, M16 x 2.0 x 70-mm, class 10.9</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Mounting Plate, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375194</td><td>Engine stand</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163820</td><td>Thread insert*</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375957</td><td>Nylon lifting sling (2000 lb.)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375958</td><td>Nylon lifting sling (4000 lb.)</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>* The threaded insert is press fit into the mounting plate and is used for repair purposes <b>only</b>.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use substitute capscrews without first verifying that they have the same specifications as the capscrews supplied in the kit. Failure to do so can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The mounting plate must be used to mount only a Signature, ISX, ISX with CM870 or QSX15 cylinder head on the engine repair stand. Improper use can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><p>Inspect the mounting plate and all capscrews for any damage, rust, wear, or missing parts. Do <b>not</b> use the mounting plate or capscrews if damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00249.png\" alt=\"22c00249.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>All eight M10 capscrews must be used and tightened to specification. Failure to do so can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><p>Install the mounting plate (1) on the exhaust manifold mounting face the of cylinder head using the eight M10 capscrews (2).</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>60 n•m [44 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00243.png\" alt=\"22c00243.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Rigging and lifting of the cylinder head must be done by trained and experienced personnel only. Do not attempt to lift the cylinder head while attached to the cylinder block. Improper use can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><p>Install one nylon lifting sling, Part Number 3375957 or Part Number 3375958, through the center valve camshaft bore. Install a second lifting sling, Part Number 3375957 or Part Number 3375958, through the center injector camshaft bore.</p><p>Connect the lifting slings to an appropriate hoist to lift the cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00244.png\" alt=\"22c00244.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>All four M16 capscrews must be used and tightened to specification. Failure to do so can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><p>Align the holes in the mounting plate with the holes in the engine repair stand. Install the four M16 capscrews through the engine repair stand plate and into the four mounting plate holes.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>150 n•m [110 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00245.png\" alt=\"22c00245.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Rigging and lifting of the cylinder head must be done by trained and experienced personnel only. Do not attempt to lift the cylinder head while attached to the cylinder block. Improper use can result in equipment damage, severe personal injury or death.</p></div></div><p>Install one nylon lifting sling, Part Number 3375957 or Part Number 3375958, through the center valve camshaft bore. Install a second lifting sling, Part Number 3375957 or Part Number 3375958, through the center injector camshaft bore.</p><p>Connect the lifting slings to an appropriate hoist and raise the hoist to put the slings in tension.</p><p>Remove the four M16 capscrews from the engine repair stand.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00245.png\" alt=\"22c00245.png\"></figure><p>Remove the eight M10 capscrews (2) and mounting plate (1) from cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00243.png\" alt=\"22c00243.png\"></figure>","3377921":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Rear Power Takeoff Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool instruction provides information for using the rear power takeoff (REPTO) replacer kit, Part Number 3164761. The REPTO replacer kit is used to remove and install the QSX15 REPTO components.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00211.png\" alt=\"22c00211.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, REPTO Replacer Kit, Part Number 3164761</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164766</td><td>Spacer</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164765</td><td>Guide pin, M16x1.5</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164764</td><td>Guide pin, M16x2.0</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3164767</td><td>Eye bolt</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3164837</td><td>Handle</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3164762</td><td>Replacer plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3925883\">3925883</a></td><td>Hex flange head capscrew</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Optional Tools, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td></td><td>Slide hammer, 1/2 x 20 thread (similar to Snap-On Part Number CJ114)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164780</td><td>Rear crankshaft seal replacer kit *</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>* The existing replacer plate, Part Number 3162995, included in the rear crankshaft seal kits, Part Number 3164153 and Part Number 3162994, can be modified by drilling three additional 17-mm [21/32-inch] holes. The six 17-mm [21/32-inch] holes are equally spaced on a 138-mm [5.433-in] bolt circle. The additional three holes update rear crankshaft seal replacer, Part Number 3162995, to the rear crankshaft seal replacer, Part Number 3164763 (included in kit, Part Number 3164780).</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>For additional information on servicing the REPTO components, refer to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>The two guide pins (3), Part Number 3164764, are used to guide the flywheel housing during removal and installation.</p><p>The two eye bolts (4), Part Number 3164767, are used to lift the flywheel housing during removal and installation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00212.png\" alt=\"22c00212.png\"></figure><p>The replacer plate (6), Part Number 3164762, handle (5), Part Number 3164837, and capscrews, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3925883\">3925883</a>, are used to install the idler shaft into the flywheel housing.</p><p>A slide hammer (similar to Snap-On Part Number CJ114) and the replacer plate (6), Part Number 3164762, are used to remove the idler shaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00213.png\" alt=\"22c00213.png\"></figure><p>The three guide pins (2), Part Number 3164765, are used to support the REPTO crankshaft gear for both the removal and installation processes.</p><p>The three spacers (1), Part Number 3164766, are placed on three flywheel mounting capscrews and the capscrews are installed into the three open holes in the REPTO crankshaft gear. Tighten the capscrews to press the crankshaft gear onto the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00214.png\" alt=\"22c00214.png\"></figure><p>The crankshaft seal is removed and installed using the rear crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 3164780. The flywheel mounting capscrews (without the spacers) are used to press the crankshaft oil seal into location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00215.png\" alt=\"22c00215.png\"></figure>","3377922":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Cylinder Head Coolant Leak Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using cylinder head coolant leak test kit, Part Number 3164917. The kit is used to leak test the cylinder head coolant passages on the Signature, ISX, ISX with CM870, and QSX15 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00219.png\" alt=\"22c00219.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Cylinder Head Coolant Leak Test Kit, Part Number 3164917</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164918</td><td>Plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164919</td><td>Gasket</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164920</td><td>Plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3164921</td><td>Gasket</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3163842</td><td>M18 x 1.5 nut</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3164195</td><td>Injector sleeve retainer</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>68138</td><td>Male connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3064106\">3064106</a></td><td>Capscrew</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3009330\">3009330</a></td><td>Washer</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Cylinder Head Coolant Leak Test Kit, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164231</td><td>Leak test kit</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3162996</td><td>Cylinder head lifting bracket</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375957</td><td>Lifting strap</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Place the cylinder head on a work bench with the intake side down.</p><p>Install the gasket (2) onto the combustion face of the cylinder head. Install the plate (1), with the marking “exhaust” toward the exhaust side of cylinder head, onto the gasket.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00228.png\" alt=\"22c00228.png\"></figure><p>Install the cylinder head capscrews and nuts (5), as illustrated. Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>68 n•m [50 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00229.png\" alt=\"22c00229.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the male connector (7) is <b>not</b> installed in the plate (3), install it now using thread sealant.</p></div></div><p>Install the gasket (4) and plate (3) onto the cylinder head thermostat location. Install the four capscrews (8) and washers (9). Tighten the capscrews</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>27 n•m [20 ft-lb]</p></div></div><p>Attach the leak test kit, Part Number 3164231, or equivalent, to the male connector (7).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00230.png\" alt=\"22c00230.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain the injector sleeve retainers are centered in the injector bore when the clamps are tightened.</p></div></div><p>Install the six injector sleeve retainers (6) into the cylinder head injector bores. Install the injector hold down clamps and capscrews. Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>41 n•m [30 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00241.png\" alt=\"22c00241.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><p>Leak Test with Dunk Tank</p><p>Use cylinder head lifting bracket, Part Number 3162996, or lifting strap, Part Number 3375957, and a hoist to lower the cylinder head into a dunk tank. Apply 207 kPa [30 psi] of air pressure. Allow several minutes for stabilization. If bubbles are present, check to make sure the plates, gaskets, and male connector are <b>not</b> leaking. If bubbles persist and are <b>not</b> attributed to the above service tools, the cylinder head <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00232.png\" alt=\"22c00232.png\"></figure><p>Leak Test without Dunk Tank</p><p>Apply 207 kPa [30 psi] of air pressure. Spray a mild soapy water solution around the six injector bores, cup plugs, exhaust ports, and entire combustion face.</p><p>Check for the presence of bubbles. If bubbles are present, check to make sure the gaskets, plates, and male connector are <b>not</b> leaking.</p><p>If bubbles persist and are <b>not</b> attributed to the above service tools, the cylinder head <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00236.png\" alt=\"22c00236.png\"></figure><p>Remove the cylinder head capscrews and nuts.</p><p>Remove the plate and gasket.</p><p>Remove the air supply hose, capscrews, washers, plate, and gasket.</p><p>Remove the six injector sleeve retainers, capscrews and hold down clamps, from the cylinder head injector bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00233.png\" alt=\"22c00233.png\"></figure>","3377924":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Cylinder Head Fuel Passage Leak Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using cylinder head fuel passage leak test kit, Part Number 3164943. The kit is used to leak test the fuel passages in the cylinder head on the Signature, ISX, ISX with CM870, and QSX15 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00221.png\" alt=\"22c00221.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Cylinder Head Fuel Passage Leak Test Kit, Part Number 3164943</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164945</td><td>Plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164946</td><td>Gasket</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164923</td><td>Injector cavity plug</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089232\">3089232</a></td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (long)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089016\">3089016</a></td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (short)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3330537\">3330537</a></td><td>O-ring seal</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3330538\">3330538</a></td><td>O-ring seal</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3347937\">3347937</a></td><td>O-ring seal</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3347939\">3347939</a></td><td>O-ring seal</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>68138</td><td>Male connector</td><td>6</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Item Used with the Cylinder Head Fuel Passage Leak Test Kit, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164231</td><td>Leak test kit</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The fuel system is split into two banks. The front bank is for cylinders one through three, and the rear bank is for cylinders four through six. For this configuration, the banks are tested independently of each other.</p><p>The left three male connectors on the plate are for the front bank and the right three male connectors are for the rear bank.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00237.png\" alt=\"22c00237.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the male connectors are <b>not</b> installed in the plate, install them now using thread sealant.</p></div></div><p>Install the gasket, plate, and the two short capscrews (5) and two long capscrews (4). Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>27 n•m [20 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00238.png\" alt=\"22c00238.png\"></figure><p>Inspect and lubricate the o-rings on the injector cavity plugs (3). Replace any worn or torn o-rings.</p><p>Install the three Injector cavity plugs (3) into either the front bank or the rear bank injector bores as required for testing.</p><p>Install the injector hold down clamps and capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>41 n•m [30 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00231.png\" alt=\"22c00231.png\"></figure><p>Attach the leak test kit, Part Number 3164231, or equivalent, to one of the three male connectors (metering, timing, or return) on the plate.</p><p>Apply 207 kPa [30 psi] of air pressure and shut off the air supply with the ball valve.</p><p>The fuel passage <b>must</b> maintain a minimum of 193 kPa [28 psi] for 30 seconds.</p><p>If 193 kPa [28 psi] is <b>not</b> maintained for 30 seconds, verify that none of the test hardware is leaking.</p><p>The <b>only</b> repair available is the replacement of the o-ring sealed plugs located at the ends of the cylinder head that terminate the fuel rail drilling. If the leaks are from any location other than these plugs, the cylinder head <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00222.png\" alt=\"22c00222.png\"></figure><p>Perform the same procedure for each of the other two passages on the bank of cylinders.</p><p>Remove the three injector cavity plugs (3) and move them to the other bank of cylinders as required for testing and repeat the above procedures.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00231.png\" alt=\"22c00231.png\"></figure>","3377926":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Front Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool instruction explains the use of the front crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 3164926. The front crankshaft seal replacer kit is used to remove and install the QSK23 engine front crankshaft seal and the dust seal (used on construction applications).</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>A new dust seal is <b>not</b> included with a new front crankshaft seal and <b>must</b> be ordered separately.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400135.png\" alt=\"22400135.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Front Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 3164926</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164972</td><td>Replacer screw assembly</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164968</td><td>Crankshaft seal replacer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163489</td><td>Round head capscrew, M22 x 1.5 x 40-mm</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3163828</td><td>Sheet metal screw, number 10 x 50.8-mm [2-in] (6 shown)</td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164218</td><td>Drill, [9/64-in]</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Mount the replacer screw assembly (1) onto the crankshaft nose.</p><p>Install the M22 x 1.5 x 60-mm round head capscrews (3).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400136.png\" alt=\"22400136.png\"></figure><p>Lubricate the replacer screw assembly with Lubriplate™, Part Number 3163086, Part Number 3163087 or a suitable grease.</p><p>Hold the replacer screw and install the crankshaft seal replacer (2) onto the replacer screw assembly.</p><p>Advance the crankshaft seal replacer toward the front seal or dust seal by rotating it <b>clockwise</b> until it is positioned against the front seal or dust seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400137.png\" alt=\"22400137.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Drill holes carefully and straight to reduce the possibility of damage to the front cover or the crankshaft.</p></div></div><p>For in chassis use, if space is restricted, use a compact right angle drill or shorten the drill bit as necessary.</p><p>Apply grease to the drill to catch the chips. Stop frequently to remove the chips. With the crankshaft seal replacer against the front seal or (dust seal on construction applications), drill one hole 10-mm [0.39 in] deep through the oil seal casing.</p><p>Install one sheet metal screw into the front seal to hold the crankshaft seal replacer in position.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400138.png\" alt=\"22400138.png\"></figure><p>Drill five additional holes 10-mm [0.39] deep and install the sheet metal screws.</p><p><b>All</b> six sheet metal screws <b>must</b> be threaded through both the dust seal (if equipped) and front seal. The sheet metal screws need to be uniformly tightened in order to pull out both seals together.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400139.png\" alt=\"22400139.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use an impact wrench or air tools. Doing so can damage the tool.</p></div></div><p>Slowly rotate the replacer screw <b>clockwise</b> until the seals are removed. Use a ratcheting box wrench such as Snap-On, Part Number RBLM1315, or equivalent to facilitate the removal and installation of the seal in a restricted space.</p><p>If the sheet metal screws pull out of the seals, stop the removal operation. Remove the sheet metal screws, reorient the crankshaft seal replacer, drill new holes, and reinstall the sheet metal screws. Complete the removal procedure, remove the replacer, and discard the oil seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400140.png\" alt=\"22400140.png\"></figure><p>Before installing both front seals, make sure the metal chips are completely removed.</p><p>Use a magnet to remove any metal chips from crankshaft.</p><p>Use a crocus cloth to polish and remove any deposits from the crankshaft. Visible scratches on the sealing surface can result in seal leakage.</p><p>Use a clean, lint-free cloth to clean the crankshaft flange and remove all traces of oil film.</p><p>Check crankshaft end for nicks, burrs, and grooves.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400163.png\" alt=\"22400163.png\"></figure><p>Using the plastic installation sleeve, place the new oil seal over the crankshaft nose and slide the seal toward the front cover. Make sure the oil seal is positioned squarely on the crankshaft. Avoid cocking the seal. Remove the plastic installation sleeve supplied with the oil seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400160.png\" alt=\"22400160.png\"></figure><p>Mount the replacer screw assembly (1) onto the crankshaft nose.</p><p>Install the M22 x 1.5 x 60-mm round head capscrews (3).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400141.png\" alt=\"22400141.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use an impact wrench or air tools. Doing so can damage the tool.</p></div></div><p>Hold the replacer screw and install the crankshaft seal replacer (2) onto the replacer screw assembly.</p><p>Advance the crankshaft seal replacer toward the front seal by rotating it <b>clockwise</b> until it is positioned against the front seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400142.png\" alt=\"22400142.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not overtighten the replacer screw assembly after the crankshaft seal replacer contacts the front cover. Doing so can damage the tool.</p></div></div><p>Holding the crankshaft seal replacer, rotate the replacer screw <b>counterclockwise</b> until the crankshaft seal replacer is positioned against the front cover.</p><p>Remove the crankshaft seal replacer from the replacer screw assembly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400143.png\" alt=\"22400143.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The dust seal <b>must</b> be ordered separate from the front seal.</p></div></div><p>Place the dust seal (used on construction applications) over the crankshaft nose and slide toward the front cover. Make sure the dust seal is positioned squarely on the crankshaft. Avoid cocking the dust seal.</p><p>Hold the replacer screw and install the crankshaft seal replacer (2) onto the replacer screw assembly. Advance the crankshaft seal replacer toward the dust seal by rotating it <b>clockwise</b> until it is positioned against the dust seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400142.png\" alt=\"22400142.png\"></figure><p>Holding the crankshaft seal replacer, rotate the replacer screw <b>counterclockwise</b> until the dust seal is positioned to the required depth.</p><p>An under cut (1) on the crankshaft seal replacer will determine the correct depth (4-mm) of the dust seal. Do <b>not</b> contact the crankshaft seal replacer against the front cover.</p><p>Remove the front crankshaft seal replacer and the replacer screw assembly.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>22400162.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/22/4/22400162.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div>","3377927":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Rear Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool instruction explains the use of the rear crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 3164927, for the QSK23 engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400125.png\" alt=\"22400125.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Rear Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 3164927</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164967</td><td>Replacer screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164966</td><td>Crankshaft seal replacer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164218</td><td>Drill, [9/64-inch]</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3164217</td><td>Sheet metal screw, number 10 x 25.4-mm [1-in] (5 shown)</td><td>36</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Lubricate the threads and tip of the replacer screw with Lubriplate™, Part Number 3163086, Part Number 3163087 or a suitable grease.</p><p>Install the replacer screw into the crankshaft seal replacer. Make sure the replacer screw tip is flush with the inside of the crankshaft seal replacer.</p><p>Position the crankshaft seal replacer against the end of the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400126.png\" alt=\"22400126.png\"></figure><p>Install one flywheel mounting capscrew through the crankshaft seal replacer into the crankshaft and finger-tighten. This will hold the replacer in position until the sheet metal screws are installed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400127.png\" alt=\"22400127.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Drill holes carefully and straight to reduce the possibility of damage to the flywheel housing or the crankshaft.</p></div></div><p>Apply grease to the drill to catch the chips. Stop frequently to remove the chips.</p><p>Drill one hole 10 mm [0.39 in] deep through the oil seal casing. Install the sheet metal screw into the hole. Drill five additional holes 10 mm [0.39 in] deep and install the sheet metal screws. Make sure all six sheet metal screws are threaded through the oil seal casing and uniformly positioned against the crankshaft seal replacer.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400128.png\" alt=\"22400128.png\"></figure><p>Remove the flywheel mounting capscrew.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400129.png\" alt=\"22400129.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use an impact wrench or air tools. Doing so can damage the tool.</p></div></div><p>Slowly rotate the replacer screw <b>clockwise</b> until the oil seal is removed.</p><p>If the sheet metal screws pull out of the seal, stop the removal operation. Remove the sheet metal screws, reorient the crankshaft seal replacer, drill new holes, and reinstall the sheet metal screws.</p><p>Complete the removal procedure, remove the replacer, and discard the oil seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400130.png\" alt=\"22400130.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Before installing the oil seal make sure all the metal chips are completely removed and the surface is clean. Failure to do so can cause engine damage.</p></div></div><p>Using the plastic installation sleeve, place the new oil seal over the rear crankshaft nose and slide the oil seal toward the flywheel housing. Make sure the oil seal is positioned squarely on the crankshaft. Avoid cocking the seal. Remove the plastic installation sleeve supplied with the oil seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400131.png\" alt=\"22400131.png\"></figure><p>Remove the replacer screw from the crankshaft seal replacer.</p><p>Position the replacer over the crankshaft and against the oil seal.</p><p>Install five flywheel mounting capscrews through the replacer into the crankshaft and uniformity finger-tighten.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400132.png\" alt=\"22400132.png\"></figure><p>Tighten the first capscrew 1/4 of a turn.</p><p>Finger-tighten the remaining capscrews. After the capscrews are finger-tight, tighten the capscrews 1/4 of a turn in an every other capscrew pattern.</p><p>Continue tightening the flywheel mounting capscrews until the crankshaft seal replacer is positioned against the crankshaft.</p><p>Remove the flywheel mounting capscrews and the replacer.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400133.png\" alt=\"22400133.png\"></figure>","3377930":"<h3>Description</h3><p>QSK23 and QSK78 Camshaft Removal and Installation Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using camshaft removal and installation kit, Part Number 3164610. The kit is used to remove and install the camshaft on the QSK23 and QSK78 engines. The camshaft pilot, Part Number 3164845, provides extra stability to the camshaft during the removal and installation procedures, and <b>must</b> be used with Part Number 3164610. The long camshaft pilot, Part Number 3164845, can also be used on the QSK45 and QSK60. The short camshaft pilot, Part Number 3163325, can be used on the QSK78 to remove and install the camshaft without removing the flywheel housing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400169.png\" alt=\"22400169.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, QSK23 and QSK78 Camshaft Removal and Installation Kit, Part Number 3164610</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164611</td><td>Camshaft guide</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3825153</td><td>Camshaft guide remover</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Table 2, Optional Items Used with the Camshaft Removal and Installation Kit, Purchased Separately</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164845</td><td>Camshaft pilot kit (long)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163325</td><td>Camshaft pilot (short)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Camshaft Pilot Kit (long), Part Number 3164845</p><p>Camshaft Pilot Kit, Part Number 3164845, used with the QSK23 and QSK78 Camshaft Removal and Installation Kit, Part Number 3164610, purchased separately</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3164701</td><td>Camshaft pilot</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163327</td><td>Pilot shaft</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>211177</td><td>O-ring</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3163323</td><td>Spacer</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3077840\">3077840</a></td><td>Socket head capscrew</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3903210\">3903210</a></td><td>Nut</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>3165109</td><td>Pilot shaft</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400168.png\" alt=\"22400168.png\"></figure><p>QSK23 Engines</p><p>Assemble the pilot shaft (7) into the camshaft pilot (1). The end with the smaller threads goes into the pilot with the keyway oriented toward the setscrew hole.</p><p>Install the socket head capscrew (5) into the setscrew hole and hand-tighten. The pilot shaft (7) <b>must</b> be free to slide back and forth over a short distance. Thread the nut (6) onto the pilot shaft (7) through the opening in the camshaft pilot (1) and do <b>not</b> tighten.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400170.png\" alt=\"22400170.png\"></figure><p>QSK78 Engines</p><p>Assemble the two o-rings (3) and two spacers (4) onto the pilot shaft (2), as illustrated. Insert the threaded end of the pilot shaft (2) into the camshaft pilot (1) with the keyway oriented toward the setscrew hole.</p><p>Install the socket head capscrew (5) into the setscrew hole and hand-tighten. The pilot shaft (2) <b>must</b> be free to slide back and forth over a short distance. Thread the nut (6) onto the pilot shaft (2) through the opening in the camshaft pilot (1) and do <b>not</b> tighten.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400171.png\" alt=\"22400171.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that the camshaft, camshaft guides, and pilot are free of lubricant and debris. Dirt particles on the inside diameter of the camshaft guides and the camshaft lobes during removal can scratch the surface of the camshaft causing performance degradation or damage to the engine.</p></div></div><p>Inspect the camshaft guides for nicks and burrs, and clean thoroughly before each use. Repair or replace damaged camshaft guides.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> lubricate the inner diameter of the camshaft guides. After installing the camshaft guides, lubricate the outer diameter with Lubriplate™, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400172.png\" alt=\"22400172.png\"></figure><p>The camshaft guides are installed on the inner base circle of the camshaft lobe, <b>not</b> the ramp of the camshaft lobe.</p><p>Use the chart below to install the camshaft guides on the appropriate exhaust and intake camshaft lobes of the QSK23 or QSK78 engine camshaft.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QSK78 Camshaft Lobes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td></tr><tr><td>Exhaust - 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9</td><td>Exhaust - 4 and 9</td></tr><tr><td>Intake - 4 and 9</td><td>Intake - 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</p><p>QSK23 Camshaft Lobes</p><p>Exhaust - 4 and 6</p><p>Intake - 1, 3, and 5</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The Camshaft Guide Installation chart is for general guidance to facilitate camshaft removal; however, placement of camshaft guides can be changed to suit existing conditions.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600011.png\" alt=\"22600011.png\"></figure><p>It will be necessary to rotate the camshaft to install the camshaft guides. Rotate the camshaft <b>only</b> when the camshaft journals are in the camshaft bushings. Do <b>not</b> rotate the camshaft when the camshaft guides are in the bushings as this can cause the camshaft to bind.</p><p>Adjust the camshaft guides until the camshaft lobe is in the middle of the camshaft guide opening. The camshaft guides <b>must</b> be positioned flush with the camshaft lobe.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600017.png\" alt=\"22600017.png\"></figure><p>QSK23 Engines</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>On QSK23 engines, the camshaft pilot is installed on the camshaft at the front of the engine.</p></div></div><p>Thread the camshaft pilot (1) with the pilot shaft (7) into the threaded camshaft hole. Do <b>not</b> tighten.</p><p>Slide the camshaft pilot and camshaft assembly rearward until the front camshaft bearing journal and the camshaft pilot are in the front bearing shell. Hand-tighten the nut (6) to secure the camshaft pilot to the camshaft.</p><p>The keyway in the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be kept at the 6-o&#x27;clock position for ease of removal with camshaft guides installed as shown.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400178.png\" alt=\"22400178.png\"></figure><p>QSK78 Engines</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When removing the camshaft with the flywheel housing installed, use short camshaft pilot, Part Number 3163325. If required for assembly, remove the dowel pin from the camshaft pilot mounting face.</p></div></div><p>Before installing the camshaft pilot (1) onto the camshaft, lightly lubricate the o-ring seals.</p><p>Install the camshaft pilot (1) flush against the camshaft. Hand-tighten the nut.</p><p>The keyway in the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be kept at the 12-o&#x27;clock position for ease of removal with camshaft guides installed as shown.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400173.png\" alt=\"22400173.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear gloves when handling the camshaft. The camshaft has sharp edges that can cause injury if not handled carefully.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not rotate the camshaft during removal. The camshaft guides can bind and make removal difficult. If necessary, it is permissible to slightly wiggle the camshaft.</p></div></div><p>Remove the camshaft until it is approximately halfway out of the cylinder block.</p><p>As the camshaft is removed, the camshaft guides that have cleared the cylinder block can be moved to other camshaft lobes still within the cylinder block if desired.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600123.png\" alt=\"22600123.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, stay clear of the camshaft when it is being raised or lowered.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the camshaft is balanced when lifting. If the camshaft is not balanced, it can fall and cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use a lifting strap secured around the camshaft to lift the camshaft slightly and support it. Lifting the camshaft too much or too little will bind the camshaft in the bore. Carefully guide the camshaft through the camshaft bore. Make certain that the camshaft is balanced on the lifting strap.</p><p>Remove the camshaft from the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600013.png\" alt=\"22600013.png\"></figure><p>After removing the camshaft, use the camshaft guide remover to remove the camshaft guides from the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600014.png\" alt=\"22600014.png\"></figure><p>Loosen the nut and remove the camshaft pilot (1) from the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400175.png\" alt=\"22400175.png\"></figure><p>QSK23 Engines</p><p>Thread the camshaft pilot (1) with pilot shaft (7) into the hole in the end of the camshaft, do <b>not</b> tighten.</p><p>The keyway in the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be kept at the 6 o&#x27;clock position for ease of installation with camshaft guides installed as shown.</p><p>QSK78 Engines</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When installing the camshaft with the flywheel housing installed, use short camshaft pilot, Part Number 3163325. If required for assembly, remove the dowel pin from the camshaft pilot mounting face.</p></div></div><p>Lubricate the o-rings before installing the camshaft pilot onto the camshaft.</p><p>Install the camshaft pilot (1) with the pilot shaft (2) against the camshaft and tighten the nut to the secure assembly.</p><p>The keyway in the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be kept at the 12 o&#x27;clock position for ease of installation with camshaft guides installed as shown.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400175.png\" alt=\"22400175.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that the camshaft, camshaft guides, and pilot are free of lubricant and debris. Dirt particles on the inside diameter of the camshaft guides and the camshaft lobes during installation can scratch the surface of the camshaft causing performance degradation or damage to the engine.</p></div></div><p>Inspect the camshaft guides for nicks and burrs, and clean thoroughly before each use. Repair or replace damaged camshaft guides.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> lubricate the inner diameter of the camshaft guides. After installing the camshaft guides, lubricate the outer diameter with Lubriplate™, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400172.png\" alt=\"22400172.png\"></figure><p>The camshaft guides are installed on the inner base circle of the camshaft lobe, <b>not</b> the ramp of the camshaft lobe.</p><p>Use the chart below to install the camshaft guides on the appropriate exhaust and intake camshaft lobes of the QSK23 or QSK78 engine camshaft.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QSK78 Camshaft Lobes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td></tr><tr><td>Exhaust - 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9</td><td>Exhaust - 4 and 9</td></tr><tr><td>Intake - 4 and 9</td><td>Intake - 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</p><p>QSK23 Camshaft Lobes</p><p>Exhaust - 4 and 6</p><p>Intake - 1, 3, and 5</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The Camshaft Guide Installation chart is for general guidance to facilitate camshaft installation; however, placement of camshaft guides can be changed to suit existing conditions.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600015.png\" alt=\"22600015.png\"></figure><p>Adjust the camshaft guides until the camshaft lobe is in the middle of the camshaft guide opening. The camshaft guides <b>must</b> be positioned flush with the camshaft journal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600074.png\" alt=\"22600074.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear gloves when handling the camshaft. The camshaft has sharp edges that can cause injury if not handled carefully.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, stay clear of the camshaft when it is being raised or lowered.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the camshaft is balanced when lifting. If the camshaft is not balanced, it can fall and cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use a lifting strap secured around the camshaft to lift it into a position parallel to the camshaft bore axis. Make certain that the camshaft is balanced on the lifting strap.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>22400176.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/22/4/22400176.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not rotate the camshaft during installation. The camshaft guides can bind and make installation difficult. If necessary, it is permissible to slightly wiggle the camshaft.</p></div></div><p>Carefully guide the camshaft into the camshaft bore. Lifting the camshaft too much or too little will bind the camshaft in the bore.</p><p>For the QSK23, slide the camshaft pilot and camshaft assembly into the rear bearing until the front bearing journal and the camshaft pilot are in the rear bearing shell. Tighten the nut (6) to secure the pilot to the camshaft.</p><p>After the camshaft has been installed halfway, the lifting strap can be removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600013.png\" alt=\"22600013.png\"></figure><p>Once the camshaft is installed, loosen the nut and remove the camshaft pilot (1) from the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400177.png\" alt=\"22400177.png\"></figure><p>Use the camshaft guide remover to remove the camshaft guides.</p><p>It will be necessary to rotate the camshaft to remove the camshaft guides. Rotate the camshaft <b>only</b> when the camshaft journals are in the camshaft bushings. Do <b>not</b> rotate the camshaft when the camshaft guides are in the bushings as this can cause the camshaft to bind.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600018.png\" alt=\"22600018.png\"></figure>","3377932":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Guide Replacer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides instructions for the valve guide replacer, Part Number 3164427. The valve guide replacer is used to remove and install the valve guides on the QSK23 and QSK78 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400149.png\" alt=\"22400149.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Valve Guide Replacer, Part Number 3164427</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164428</td><td>Valve guide installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164429</td><td>Spacer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164436</td><td>Valve guide remover</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Use an arbor press and a valve guide remover, Part Number 3164436, to remove the worn valve guide.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400150.png\" alt=\"22400150.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris or dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to avoid personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent to clean the valve guide bores.</p><p>Dry with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02a00042.png\" alt=\"02a00042.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the mandrel does not damage the top of the valve guide. If the guide is damaged, the valves can stick, causing severe engine damage.</p></div></div><p>Position the valve guide in the valve guide bore in the cylinder head.</p><p>Slide the spacer, Part Number 3164429, over the valve guide. Use an arbor press and a valve guide installer, Part Number 3164428, to press the guide into the cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400151.png\" alt=\"22400151.png\"></figure>","3377933":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Stem Seal Installer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides instructions for the valve stem seal installer, Part Number 3164430. The valve stem seal installer is used to install the valve seal on the QSK23 and QSK78 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400158.png\" alt=\"22400158.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Valve Stem Seal Installer, Part Number 3164430</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164431</td><td>Valve stem seal installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164432</td><td>Spacer</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Valve Stem Seal Installer, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163293</td><td>Boot pliers</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Remove the valve stem seal with the boot pliers, Part Number 3163293, using a twist-and-pull motion.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400146.png\" alt=\"22400146.png\"></figure><p>Make sure the valve guide and valve stem seal are clean and dry before installation.</p><p>Apply Lubriplate™ on the stem.</p><p>Install the new valve stem seal on the valve stem. Push the valve stem seal down until contact is made with the top of the valve guide.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400147.png\" alt=\"22400147.png\"></figure><p>Slide the spacer, Part Number 3164432, over the valve stem and down over the valve guide.</p><p>Using a plastic mallet and the valve stem seal installer, Part Number 3164431, gently tap the valve seal into place.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400148.png\" alt=\"22400148.png\"></figure>","3377934":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Lubricating Oil Cooler Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for lubricating oil cooler test kit, Part Number 4918200. The kit is used to test the oil cooler assembly for leakage. For additional information on the use of the kit, refer to Procedure 007-003 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Base Engine Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin Number <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00251.png\" alt=\"22c00251.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Lubricating Oil Cooler Test Kit, Part Number 4918200</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918201</td><td>Outlet cover plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918203</td><td>Inlet cover plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4918204</td><td>Filter head cap</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089567\">3089567</a></td><td>Threaded plug</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3049221\">3049221</a></td><td>O-ring seal, 1-1/8 inch (inside diameter)</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>68642</td><td>O-ring seal, 1-3/4 inch (inside diameter)</td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with Lubricating Oil Cooler Test Kit, Part Number 4918200, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164231</td><td>Air pressure regulator</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377935":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Gear Remover</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool bulletin provides instructions for the front crankshaft gear remover, Part Number 3165049. The crankshaft gear remover will remove the crankshaft gear from the crankshaft without heating the gear. The crankshaft gear remover is used on K19, QSK19, K38, K50, V28, V903, V504, V555, N855, L10, M11, ISM, QSM11, N14, and QSK23 series engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400156.png\" alt=\"22400156.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Crankshaft Gear Remover, Part Number 3165049</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165050</td><td>Gear remover assembly</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3376833</td><td>Remover screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165051</td><td>Clevis pin</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3165052</td><td>Handle</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3375841</td><td>Straight pin</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>S-509</td><td>Cotter pin (3/32x1)</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Crankshaft Gear Remover, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3375835</td><td>Remover jaw (K19, K38, K50, QSK19, and QSK23)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3375836</td><td>Remover jaw (V28)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3375837</td><td>Remover jaw (V903)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3375838</td><td>Remover jaw (V504 and V555)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3375839</td><td>Remover jaw (N855, L10, M11, ISM, and QSM11)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3824284</td><td>Remover jaw (N14)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377936":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Electrical Circuit Tester Kits</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool instruction provides procedures for using the electrical circuit tester kit, Part Numbers 3163594 or 3163878. The electrical circuit tester, Part Number 3163589, is portable and allows the technician to monitor voltage, current, and open circuits in the ECM harness at the ECM pins. The electrical circuit tester, Part Number 3163878, <b>only</b> allows the technician to monitor voltage in the harness and is <b>not</b> shown in the illustration below.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do <b>not</b> operate vehicle while tool is in use.</p></div></div><p>Both electrical circuit tester kits include an electrical circuit tester, harness adapter cable (10 feet), and ECM connector adapter cable (10 feet). The electrical circuit tester kits allow the technician to work on the following engines: ISB, ISC, ISL, ISM, ISX, Signature, QSB, QSC, QSL, and QSX. Optional adapter cables are available for power generation, Quantum™/CENSE™, and CELECT™/CELECT™ Plus.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00083.png\" alt=\"22a00083.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Electrical Circuit Tester Kit, Part Number 3163594</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3163589</td><td>Electrical circuit tester</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163590</td><td>Harness adapter cable (3048 mm [10 ft])</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163591</td><td>ECM adapter cable (3048 mm [10 ft])</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163953</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with Electrical Circuit Tester Kit, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3163880</td><td>Power generation adapter kit (see page 2)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3163883</td><td>Quantum™/CENSE™ adapter kit (see page 2)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3163886</td><td>CELECT™/CELECT™ Plus adapter kit (see page 2)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163878</td><td>Electrical circuit tester kit (see page 2)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164182</td><td>ISB with CM850, ISX/Signature with CM870 adapter kit</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>When using the electrical circuit tester kits for the power command control II kit, generator drive control system kit, or power generation adapter kit, it will be necessary to purchase the power generation adapter kit.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3163592</td><td>Harness adapter, 50-pin D-sub</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163593</td><td>ECM adapter, 50-pin D-sub</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163881</td><td>Harness adapter, 25-pin D-sub</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3163882</td><td>ECM adapter, 25-pin D-sub</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00093.png\" alt=\"22a00093.png\"></figure><p>When using the electrical circuit tester kits for the QST30 generator drive or QSK19, QSK45, QSK60, and CENSE™, it will be necessary to purchase the Quantum™/CENSE™ adapter kit.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3163884</td><td>Harness adapter, 40-pin Deutsch connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163885</td><td>ECM adapter, 40-pin Deutsch connector</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00094.png\" alt=\"22a00094.png\"></figure><p>When using the electrical circuit tester kits for the CELECT™ or CELECT™ Plus system, it will be necessary to purchase the CELECT™/CELECT™ Plus adapter kit.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3163887</td><td>Harness adapter, 28-pin AMP connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163888</td><td>ECM adapter, 28-pin AMP connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163961</td><td>Harness adapter, 28-pin AMP connector</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00095.png\" alt=\"22a00095.png\"></figure><p>This electrical circuit tester kit is used to monitor voltage <b>only</b> in the wiring harness.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3163879</td><td>Electrical circuit tester</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163590</td><td>Adapter cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163591</td><td>Adapter cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163953</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22100101.png\" alt=\"22100101.png\"></figure><p>When using the electrical circuit tester kits on the 60-pin engine connector on the ISB with the CM 850 or ISX with the CM 870, it will be necessary to purchase adapter kit, Part Number 3164182.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3164184</td><td>Harness adapter, 60-pin Deutsch connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164183</td><td>ECM adapter, 60-pin Deutsch connector</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00094.png\" alt=\"22a00094.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To avoid personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To avoid arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first, and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><p>Disconnect the battery cables, negative (-) cable first.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19802564.png\" alt=\"19802564.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To avoid severe ECM damage, refer to the appropriate wiring diagram to make certain the pin is located properly.</p></div></div><p>When disconnecting the ECM, refer to the appropriate wiring diagram to identify the correct ECM connector.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00084.png\" alt=\"22a00084.png\"></figure><p>Remove the capscrew that holds the connector to the ECM.</p><p>Remove the connector.</p><p>Install the connector to the harness adapter cable.</p><p>Refer to the parts list at the beginning of this instruction for the correct adapter cable part number.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00086.png\" alt=\"22a00086.png\"></figure><p>Connect the ECM adapter cable to the ECM.</p><p>Refer to the parts list at the beginning of this instruction for the correct ECM adapter cable part number.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00087.png\" alt=\"22a00087.png\"></figure><p>Connect the ECM adapter cable from the ECM to the electrical circuit tester.</p><p>Connect the harness adapter cable from the engine harness to the electrical circuit tester.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00088.png\" alt=\"22a00088.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To avoid personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To avoid arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first, and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><p>Reconnect the battery cables, negative (-) cable last.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19802564.png\" alt=\"19802564.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To avoid severe ECM damage, refer to the appropriate wiring diagram to make certain the pin is located properly.</p></div></div><p>Use a multimeter and the electrical circuit tester, Part Number 3163589 or Part Number 3163879, to measure the voltage on a specific pin. Place the positive (+) meter lead in the desired pin. Find a ground (-) on the electrical circuit tester using the appropriate wiring diagram.</p><p>Set the toggle switch to the CLOSED position. This <b>only</b> applies to the electrical circuit tester, Part Number 3163589.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00090.png\" alt=\"22a00090.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To avoid severe ECM damage, refer to the appropriate wiring diagram to make certain the pin is located properly.</p></div></div><p>Use a multimeter and the electrical circuit tester, Part Number 3163589, to measure the amperage on a specific pin.</p><p>Place the positive (+) meter lead in the desired pin&#x27;s left test point; then place the negative (-) meter lead in the desired pin&#x27;s right test point.</p><p>Set the toggle switch to the OPEN position.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00091.png\" alt=\"22a00091.png\"></figure>","3377937":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Adapter and Gear Remover Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the Crankshaft Adapter and Gear Remover Kit, Part Number 4918530. The kit is used to remove the crankshaft adapter and gear from the crankshaft. For addition information, refer to Procedures <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/10-001-017\">001-017</a> and <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/10-001-018\">001-018</a> in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00255.png\" alt=\"22c00255.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Crankshaft Adapter and Gear Remover Kit, Part Number 4918530</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918276</td><td>Adapter, remover</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918314</td><td>Gauge, locating</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4918532</td><td>Cutter, [19.05 mm] 0.75 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4918533</td><td>Drill bit, [6.35 mm] 0.25 inch (carbide tipped bit)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4918534</td><td>Bushing, drill [11.506 mm] 0.453 inch (used with 4918544)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4918535</td><td>Drill bit, [12.70 mm] 0.50 inch (carbide tipped bit)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4918536</td><td>Drill bit, [19.05 mm] 0.75 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4918537</td><td>Drill bit, [25.4 mm] 1.00 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>4918538</td><td>Bushing, drill [6.35 mm] 0.25 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>4918539</td><td>Bushing, drill [12.70 mm] 0.50 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>4918540</td><td>Bushing, drill [19.05 mm] 0.75 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>4918541</td><td>Collar, stop [6.35 mm] 0.25 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>4918542</td><td>Collar, stop [12.70 mm] 0.50 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>4918543</td><td>Collar, stop [19.05 mm] 0.75 inch</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>4918544</td><td>Extension (used with 4918578)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>4918545</td><td>Remover (small splitting wedge)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>4918546</td><td>Remover (large splitting wedge)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>4918548</td><td>Screw, lock (removable bushing lock)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>4918577</td><td>Pin, [6.35 mm] 0.25 inch (alignment tool)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>4918578</td><td>Cutter, countersink</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>4918582</td><td>Guide, centering (plastic drill guide)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>4918593</td><td>Screw, socket set (brass tipped, used with 4918276)</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Crankshaft Adapter and Gear Remover Kit, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3823532</td><td>Drill, heavy duty right angle</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377943":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Camshaft Bushing Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using the camshaft bushing replacer kit, Part Number 3165045. The kit is used to remove and install the camshaft bushings on 4B, B3.9, 6B, B5.9, ISB (4 cylinder), ISB e (4 and 6 cylinder), QSB5.9-44, ISC, QSC8.3, G5.9, B5.9G, B5.9LPG, B Gas Plus, B LPG Plus, C8.3G, C Gas Plus, 6C, C8.3, ISL, QSL9, G3.9, B4.5 s, B6.7 s, QSB3.9-30, QSB4.5-30, QSB5.9-30 series engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000075.png\" alt=\"22000075.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Camshaft Bushing Replacer Kit, Part Number 3165045</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165038</td><td>Camshaft bushing replacer (B-series)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3165040</td><td>Camshaft bushing replacer (C-series)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165044</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3165042</td><td>Socket set screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3165063</td><td>Centering guide</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3165064</td><td>Drive bar</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>3165065</td><td>Drive bar extension</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>3165067</td><td>Hex wrench</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>3165068</td><td>Socket head capscrew</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Review the orientation of the oil holes prior to bushing removal for assembly information.</p><p>Remove the camshaft bushings using the camshaft bushing replacer kit, Part Number 3165045. Slide the drive bar through the centering guide and insert the drive bar from the rear of the cylinder block through the camshaft bores.</p><p>Install the appropriate camshaft bushing replacer and drive the front camshaft bushing from the cylinder block. Remove the replacer and remove the drive bar from the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000006.png\" alt=\"22000006.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>For engines with a single bushing proceed to the next step.</p></div></div><p>Insert the drive bar, camshaft bushing replacer, and centering guide from the front of the cylinder block. Drive the remaining camshaft bushings from the cylinder block in succession, starting with camshaft bushing number two.</p><p>Remove the drive bar, replacer, and guide from the front of the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000007.png\" alt=\"22000007.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean and inspect the cylinder block camshaft bore for excessive wear. Refer to the appropriate Troubleshooting and Repair Manual.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900070.png\" alt=\"22900070.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some camshaft bushings contain multiple oil holes. Make certain the orientation of these holes match the orientation prior to disassembly.</p></div></div><p>Mark the camshaft bushing and cylinder block using a felt pen. This will align the lubricating oil hole in the cylinder block to the oil hole in the camshaft bushing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000009.png\" alt=\"22000009.png\"></figure><p>Use the drive bar, centering guide, and appropriate camshaft bushing replacer. Slide the camshaft bushing on the replacer. Align the marks on the camshaft bushing and the cylinder block.</p><p>Drive the front camshaft bushing to the correct installed depth. The correct installed depth is when the camshaft bushing oil hole aligns with the cylinder block oil hole.</p><p>Install the remaining camshaft bushings in succession, starting at the rear of the cylinder block and working toward the front. Remove the drive bar, replacer, and guide from the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000008.png\" alt=\"22000008.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, all camshaft bushings must be checked for proper oil hole alignment after installation.</p></div></div><p>Make certain that the oil holes are aligned.</p><p>A 3.2-mm [0.126-in] diameter rod <b>must</b> pass freely through the lubricating oil hole.</p><p>Measure the camshaft bushing inside diameter. Refer to the appropriate service manual for specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg9bswd.png\" alt=\"cg9bswd.png\"></figure>","3377944":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Head Thickness Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using valve head thickness gauge, Part Number 3164984. The gauge is used to determine if the QSK19, QSK45, and QSK60 intake and exhaust valve can be reused after reconditioning.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600215.png\" alt=\"22600215.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Valve Head Thickness Gauge, Part Number 3164984</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164984</td><td>Valve head thickness gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The intake and exhaust valve face and seating surfaces <b>must</b> be cleaned and free of carbon deposits before the inspection is performed. Use Scotch-Brite 7448, Part Number 3823258, or equivalent, to clean the valve.</p><p>The valve head thickness gauge, Part Number 3164984, is used to check the intake and exhaust valve head thickness.</p><p>Place the valve into the valve head thickness gauge.</p><p>Measure the valve height. If the valve is flush or above the gauging surface, the valve can be reused. If the valve is below the gauging surface, the valve can <b>not</b> be reused.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600216.png\" alt=\"22600216.png\"></figure>","3377945":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Inspection Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This service tool instruction provides information for the inspection gauge, Part Number 3165071. This inspection gauge is used to inspect the ISX cylinder head for reuse.</p><p>For the inspection procedures, refer to Procedure 002-004 in the ISX Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00227.png\" alt=\"22c00227.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Inspection Gauge, Part Number 3165071</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>3165071</td><td>Inspection gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377947":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Wear Sleeve Installer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using the crankshaft wear sleeve installer, Part Number 3165112. The front crankshaft wear sleeve/seal kit, Part Number 3925343, is used to salvage the crankshaft with grooves worn in the oil seal area on C8.3, C8.3G, ISC, QSC8.3, ISL, and QSL9 engines. This tool installs the front crankshaft wear sleeve to the proper depth.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00183.png\" alt=\"22d00183.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Crankshaft Wear Sleeve Installer, Part Number 3165112</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164598</td><td>Capscrew</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164599</td><td>Spacer, 5/8-inch length</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165111</td><td>Installer plate</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The previous installer, Part Number 3824501, installed the 0.984-inch wide wear sleeve on C8.3, C8.3G, ISC, and QSC8.3 engines. Part Number 3165112 supersedes the previous installer and is used on ISL and QSL9 as well as C8.3, C8.3G, and ISC engines.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not nick or gouge the crankshaft with the chisel. If the crankshaft is damaged, it must be replaced.</p></div></div><p>Remove the seal carrier and/or front cover, refer to the appropriate Troubleshooting and Repair Manual.</p><p>If a wear sleeve is present, use a hammer and a bull chisel <b>only</b> as wide as the wear sleeve. Make one or two blows with a hammer to make chisel marks across the wear sleeve. Repeat this procedure at two or three locations around the circumference of the sleeve. This will expand the wear sleeve, allowing the sleeve to be removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07d00012.png\" alt=\"07d00012.png\"></figure><p>For proper sealing of the crankshaft oil seal, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be free of major damage.</p><p>Use a crocus cloth to remove any rust or other deposits from the crankshaft flange area.</p><p>Use a clean cloth to clean the crankshaft flange area.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks900ek.png\" alt=\"ks900ek.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Three capscrews are required for ISL and QSL9 engines.</p></div></div><p>Apply a thin coat of clean 15W-40 engine oil on the inside diameter of the installer plate and capscrew threads.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks9tola.png\" alt=\"ks9tola.png\"></figure><p>Gasket sealant between the wear sleeve and crankshaft is <b>not</b> recommended.</p><p>Apply a thin coat of clean 15W-40 engine oil on the crankshaft flange.</p><p>Position the chamfered end of the wear sleeve onto the end of the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00184.png\" alt=\"22d00184.png\"></figure><p>Position the counterbore end of the installer plate onto the wear sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00185.png\" alt=\"22d00185.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Three capscrews are required for ISL and QSL9 engines.</p></div></div><p>Install the capscrews (1), without the spacers, through the installer plate and into the crankshaft holes.</p><p>Align the wear sleeve and installer plate perpendicular with the crankshaft.</p><p>Finger tighten the capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00186.png\" alt=\"22d00186.png\"></figure><p>To prevent wear sleeve damage from binding and irregular stretch, do <b>not</b> exceed 1/2 revolution on each capscrew.</p><p>Alternately tighten the capscrews until the wear sleeve is installed approximately 16 mm [0.63 in].</p><p>Remove the capscrews and add the spacers.</p><p>Continue to alternately tighten the capscrews until the installer plate contacts the end of the crankshaft. Do <b>not</b> exceed the recommended torque value.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>20 n•m [15 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22900077.png\" alt=\"22900077.png\"></figure>","3377949":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Fuel Sight Glass Assembly</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information describing available fuel sight glass assemblies. Fuel sight glass assemblies are used to check for air leaks in the suction side of the fuel system. The fuel sight glass assembly illustrated below is generic and will vary with hose application.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800573.png\" alt=\"22800573.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Fuel Sight Glass Assembly, Part Number 3165147</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165147</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 20 o-ring face seal</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Other Fuel Sight Glass Assemblies, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164383</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 10 SAE</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375362</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 12 SAE</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3376718</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 12 JIC (Joint Industry Conference)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3375808</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 16 JIC (Joint Industry Conference)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164387</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 12 o-ring face seal</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163270</td><td>Fuel sight glass assembly, number 16 o-ring face seal</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Items Used with Fuel Sight Glass Assembly, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3332160\">3332160</a></td><td>O-ring face seal, number 20 (replacement for Part Number 3165147)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3075658\">3075658</a></td><td>O-ring face seal, number 16 (replacement for Part Number 3163270)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3328589\">3328589</a></td><td>O-ring face seal, number 12 (replacement for Part Number 3164387)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165146</td><td>Hose (used with 3164387 for QSK23)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377951":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Temperature Indicator Marker</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using the temperature indicator markers. The markers are used to indicate the exhaust port temperature on the QSK19, QSK23, QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 Series Engines.</p><p>QSK19, refer to Procedure</p><p>006-026</p><p>in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual QSK19 Series Engines, Bulletin 3666098.</p><p>QSK23, refer to Procedure</p><p>006-026</p><p>in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual QSK23 Series Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021375\">4021375</a>.</p><p>QSK45 and QSK60, refer to Procedure</p><p>006-026</p><p>in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual QSK45 and QSK60 Series Engines, Bulletin 3666261.</p><p>QSK78, refer to Procedure</p><p>006-026</p><p>in the CENSE™ System QSK78 Engine Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666753.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200153.png\" alt=\"22200153.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Temperature Indicator Marker, Part Number 3165163</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165163</td><td>Temperature indicator marker 204°C [400°F]</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165164</td><td>Temperature indicator marker 427°C [800°F]</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165165</td><td>Temperature indicator marker 621°C [1150°F]</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377954":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Gauge Mounting Base</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using gauge mounting base, Part Number 3165168. The base is used with dial indicator gauge, Part Number 3375006, to verify the wastegate actuator travel on the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00246.png\" alt=\"22c00246.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Gauge Mounting Base, Part Number 3165168</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165162</td><td>Gauge mounting base</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3165167</td><td>Magnet</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Gauge Mounting Base, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3375006</td><td>Dial indicator gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Install the gauge mounting base and dial indicator gauge assembly onto the wastegate cover with the dial indicator gauge tip resting on the end of the wastegate lever.</p><p>Refer to Procedure 010-050 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a> to verify the required wastegate actuator travel.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00140.png\" alt=\"10c00140.png\"></figure>","3377958":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Differential Pressure Tester</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the Differential Pressure Tester, Part Number 3824223. The tester is used with the appropriate leak test adapter to check individual cylinders to help locate sources of leaks or excessive blowby. The tester measures the leakdown rate of the cylinder by comparing the inlet pressure, (left hand gauge), with the pressure in the cylinder, (right hand gauge). The results from each cylinder are compared with each other to determine the relative blowby.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22s00006.png\" alt=\"22s00006.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Differential Pressure Tester, Part Number 3824223</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3824223</td><td>Differential pressure tester</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3164626</td><td>Quick disconnect air fitting</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Leak Test Adapter (with O-rings), Used with the Differential Pressure Tester, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3824224</td><td>Leak test adapter (K19, K38, and K50)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4918149</td><td>Leak test adapter (QSK19, QSK45, QSK60, QSK23, and QSK78)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>5298826</td><td>Leak test adapter, natural gas engines with 14-mm spark plug threads (ISX12 G CM2180 EJ, G3.9, G5.9, GTA5.9, G8.3, GTA8.3, G855, GTA855, G14, GTA12, GTA19, QSK19G, GTA28, GTA38, and GTA50) This 18 inch long adapter obsoletes and supersedes the 12 inch long Part Number 4918177 adapter. The 12 inch adapter will work properly on all of the engines listed, EXCEPT for the ISX12 G CM2180 EJ, which will require the 18 inch long adapter.</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4918178</td><td>Leak test adapter, natural gas engines with 18-mm spark plug threads (KTA19GC, QSK45G, QSK60G, QSV81, and QSV91)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4918619</td><td>Leak test adapter (QSK19, QSK38, QSK50, and QSK60 with Modular Common Rail System)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>5298630</td><td>Leak test adapter (ISB5.9, QSB5.9, ISB6.7, QSB6.7, QSB4.5, and ISB4.5)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>5299462</td><td>Leak test adapter (ISV5.0)(contains 1pr of adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Replacement O-rings Used with the Leak Test Adapter, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3010510\">3010510</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 3824224)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3201125\">3201125</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 3824224)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3347939\">3347939</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918149)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3867651\">3867651</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918149)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4010577\">4010577</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918149)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3347937\">3347937</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918149)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3066938\">3066938</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 5298826)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3201125\">3201125</a></td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918178)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>4918668</td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918619)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>4918667</td><td>O-ring (leak test adapter 4918619)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3377959":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Injector Sleeve Remover</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>The injector sleeve remover, Part Number 3377079, is used to remove the injector sleeve from the cylinder head with the use of an impact wrench. The remover can be used on the NH, V28, L10, V903, V504, and V55 series engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800545.png\" alt=\"22800545.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Injector Sleeve Remover, Part Number 3377079</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3377089</td><td>Remover nut</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3377091</td><td>Remover body</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3377095</td><td>End stop (all except small V)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3377093</td><td>Small collet (all except NH 5-1/8 inch)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3377096</td><td>End stop (small V)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3377097</td><td>Large collet (NH 5-1/8 inch)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>3377090</td><td>Thrust bearing kit</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3377092</td><td>Circlip</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3377094</td><td>Remover screw</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Lubricate the remover thrust bearing and threads with a heavy grease.</p><p>Place the remover, with the appropriate collet and end stop, into the injector bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800546.png\" alt=\"22800546.png\"></figure><p>The collet is properly seated when the end stop bottoms in the injector sleeve.</p><p>If the end stop does <b>not</b> bottom in the injector sleeve, a soft face hammer can be used to seat the collet.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800547.png\" alt=\"22800547.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>With some engine applications, the remover collet can rotate. If the collet rotates, apply pressure to the top of the collet while operating the impact wrench. Once the collet grips the injector sleeve, the pressure can be removed.</p></div></div><p>Using an impact wrench and the appropriate socket, turn the remover nut in a <b>clockwise</b> direction until the injector sleeve is removed from the cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800548.png\" alt=\"22800548.png\"></figure><p>Remove the injector sleeve from the injector sleeve remover.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If necessary, tap the injector sleeve on a workbench to release the collet from the sleeve.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800549.png\" alt=\"22800549.png\"></figure>","3377996":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Insert Remover</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for using various valve insert removers. The removers are used with slide hammer remover, Part Number 3376617, to remove valve inserts from cylinder heads. Without damaging the heads. Some engine applications have cylinder heads with valve inserts that do <b>not</b> have a groove for the remover. If there is <b>not</b> a groove for the remover, it may be necessary to use the valve insert cutter kit, Part Number 3376405, to cut a groove into the valve insert to allow for the use of the valve insert remover.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>QSK95 insert removers do <b>not</b> require use of the cutter kit.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22100097.png\" alt=\"22100097.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1 - Valve Insert Removers</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Engine Application</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ST 1276-1</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>ISX (Exhaust), NH (5 1/8 Bore), C8.3 (2 Valve Intake)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ST 1277-1</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>V6-140, V8-185, V504, V555, QSZ (Exhaust)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ST 1278-1</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>C and J Series</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ST 1279-1</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>ISX (Intake), N14, NT, V6-200, V8- 265, V903, V28, QST30</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ST 1323-1</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>K19 (Exhaust), K38 (Exhaust), K50 (Exhaust), QSK23, QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376146</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>L10, QSZ (Intake)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3824781</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>L10 and M11 (1995 and later)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3377396</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>C8.3 (2 valve, Exhaust)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165113</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>ISC and ISL (4 valve, Intake)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165114</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>ISC and ISL (4 valve, Exhaust)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3376799</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>K19 (Intake), K38 (Intake), K50 (Intake), QSK45 (Exhaust), QSK60 (Exhaust), QSK19</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165169</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>B Series (2 valve, Exhaust)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165170</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>ISB and ISD (4 Valve), ISF3.8</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165185</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>B Series (2 valve, Intake)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918189</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>QSK45 (Intake), QSK60 (Intake), QSK45G, QSK60G</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892225</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>QSK95 (Intake)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892226</td><td>Valve Insert Remover</td><td>QSK95 (Exhaust)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2 - Used with Valve Insert Removers, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3376617</td><td>Slide Hammer Remover</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>3376405</td><td>Valve Insert Cutting Kit</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>3376406</td><td>Valve Insert Cutter</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>3376407</td><td>Cutter Bit</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400193":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Air Compressor Adapter Replacer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for air compressor adapter replacer, Part Number 3165100 and other similar replacers. The replacers are used to replace the bearing retainer nut on Cummins air compressors. For additional information on the use of the replacers, refer to the appropriate OEM (original equipment manufacturer) service manual. The appropriate replacers are used on the 6B, B5.9, B5.9G, B5.9LPG, B5.9 Gas Plus, B5.9LPG Plus, ISB, ISB e 4 cylinder, ISB e 6 cylinder, C8.3G, 6C, C8.3, ISC, ISL, Signature, ISX, ISM, ISM e, V28, QSK19, K19, K19G, QSK19G, K38, K50, QST30, QSK45, QSK60, QSK60G, and QSK45G engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the splines on the replacer exhibit excessive wear, cracks, chipped or broken teeth, replace immediately. (See table 3 for the appropriate spline.)</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400208.png\" alt=\"22400208.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Air Compressor Adapter Replacer</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165100</td><td>Air compressor adapter replacer (9 tooth)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Other Air Compressor Adapter Replacers, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3165101</td><td>Air compressor adapter replacer (11 tooth)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165102</td><td>Air compressor adapter replacer (13 tooth)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3165103</td><td>Air compressor adapter replacer (3 jaw keyed)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Replacement Splines, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4918179</td><td>9 tooth replacement spline</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4918181</td><td>11 tooth replacement spline</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4918183</td><td>13 tooth replacement spline</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400198":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Fuel Pump Mounting Support Socket</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for fuel pump mounting support socket, Part Number 4918270. The socket is used to hold the driveshaft while removing the retaining nut on the QST30 engine. For additional information, refer to Procedure 009-040 in the Shop Manual, QST30 Series Engine, Bulletin 3666190.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00154.png\" alt=\"22a00154.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Fuel Pump Mounting Support Socket, Part Number 4918270</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918270</td><td>Fuel Pump Mounting Support Socket</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400205":"<h3>Description</h3><p>INLINE™ 5 Data Link Adapter Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the INLINE™ 5 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 4918416, and the associated cables to connect a personal computer to the data link adapter. The INLINE™ 5 data link adapter is designed for use with the SAE J1708 and J1939 standard protocols. The INLINE™ 5 data link adapter is used with software applications such as INSITE™ electronic service tool 6.3 and later versions, to communicate with the B5.9G, B5.9LPG, B Gas Plus, B LPG Plus, ISB, ISB e (4 and 6 cylinder), QSB3.9-30, QSB4.5-30, QSB5.9-30, QSB5.9 Marine, QSB5.9-44, C Gas Plus, ISC, QSC8.3, L10, L10 Gas, ISL, QSL9, L Gas Plus, M11, N14, Signature™, ISX, QSX15, ISM, ISM e, QSM11, QSK19, QSK19G, QSK23, QST30, QSK45, QSK45G, QSK60, QSK60G, and QSK78 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200156.png\" alt=\"22200156.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, INLINE™ 5 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 4918416</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3165033</td><td>INLINE™ 5 data link adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918419</td><td>USB cable, (2 M [6.56 feet])</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165160</td><td>Data link cable (DB25F 6-Pin Deutsch™ connector)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3165159</td><td>Data link cable (DB25F 9-Pin Deutsch™ connector)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165143</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>4918417</td><td>INLINE™ 5 software compact disc</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>4918418</td><td>DB9F-DB9M serial cable, (1.83 M [6 feet])</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>4918436</td><td>INLINE™ 4 and 5 ruggedized protective boot</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with INLINE™ 5 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 4918416, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4918857</td><td>Data link cable (DB25F 16-Pin OBD II connector)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165141</td><td>DB25F 2-Pin Weather-Pack™ and 3-Pin Deutsch™ with Cigarette Plug connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3824440</td><td>DB25F 8-Pin AMP™ connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163096</td><td>J1939 backbone adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3163597</td><td>J1939 gender change adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3165017</td><td>Palm™ universal cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3162850</td><td>DB9F-DB9M serial cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>4918591</td><td>USB cable, (5 M [16.4 feet])</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>A fully populated USB cable, Part Number 4918419, or DB9F-DB9M, serial cable, Part Number 4918418, <b>must</b> be used.</p></div></div><p>Connect the DB9F-DB9M serial cable, Part Number 4918418, or USB cable, Part Number 4918419 to the RS-232 serial port or the USB port of the computer and to the INLINE™ 5 data link adapter, Part Number 3165033.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200157.png\" alt=\"22200157.png\"></figure><p>The INLINE™ 5 data link adapter requires +8-VDC to +50-VDC at 250mA that can be supplied through the OEM connector or by a separate power source.</p><p>Connect the appropriate data link cable to the INLINE™ 5 data link adapter, Part Number 3165033.</p><p>With the data link cable connected to the INLINE™ 5 data link adapter, connect the other end of the data link cable to the vehicle cab or engine compartment data link connector.</p><p>Launch the electronic service tool application software.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200158.png\" alt=\"22200158.png\"></figure><ul><li>Power Lamp When the power lamp is continuously illuminated, DC power is being supplied to the adapter at the proper voltage level. The INLINE™ 5 data link adapter requires +8-VDC to +50-VDC at 250mA that can be supplied through the OEM connector or by a separate power source. When the power lamp is flashing, improper DC power is being supplied to the adapter. A slow flashing power lamp indicates voltage is less than +8-VDC. A fast flashing power lamp indicates voltage is greater than +50-VDC. If the power lamp is <b>not</b> illuminated, check for power at the vehicle connector and check for correct polarity.</li><li>J1939 Lamp A J1939 fast flashing lamp indicates the adapter is connected to a J1939 data link, the vehicle key switch is in the ON position, and communications are being received. A J1939 slow flashing lamp indicates the adapter is transmitting over a J1939 data link, but is <b>not</b> receiving any messages.</li><li>J1708 Lamp A J1708 fast flashing lamp indicates the adapter is connected to a J1708 data link, the vehicle key switch is in the ON position, and communications are being received. A J1708 slow flashing lamp indicates the adapter is transmitting over a J1708 data link, but is <b>not</b> receiving any messages.</li><li>RS-232 Lamp A RS-232 fast flashing lamp indicates the adapter is connected to a RS-232 port, the vehicle key switch is in the ON position, and communications are being received. A RS-232 slow flashing lamp indicates the adapter is transmitting over a RS-232 port, but is <b>not</b> receiving any messages.</li><li>USB Lamp A USB fast flashing lamp indicates the adapter is connected to a USB port, the vehicle key switch is in the ON position, and communications are being received. A USB slow flashing lamp indicates the adapter is transmitting over a USB port, but is <b>not</b> receiving any messages.</li></ul>","3400218":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Fuel Pump Lifting Fixture Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Fuel Pump Lifting Fixture Kit, Part Number 5299015. The kit is used to remove and install the fuel pump on the QSK38, QSK50, and QSK60 engines with the modular common rail fuel (MCRS) system.</p><p>Lifting fixture, Part Number 4918603, requires component kit, Part Number 5299014, when used with the QSK50 and QSK 60 engines.</p><p>Additional information for the QSK38 and QSK50 engines can be found in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></p><p>Additional information for the QSK60 engine can be found in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></p><p>The winch drive adapter, Part Number 4918662, is offered as an alternative to the winch handle in cases where a rotational obstruction exists. If the winch drive adapter is to be used, remove the retaining nut, the spring from the winch handle shaft, and the winch handle. Thread the adapter into position, then install the spring and retaining nut.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The spring and retaining nut are required for proper winch operation and can <b>not</b> be altered or permanently removed.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600344.png\" alt=\"22600344.png\"></figure><p>Fuel Pump Lifting Fixture Kit, Part Number 5299015</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item Number</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th><th>Available to Purchase</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>4918597</td><td>Mounting plate</td><td>1</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918601</td><td>Spacer [37.08 mm] 1.46 inch (QSK38 industrial)</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4918614</td><td>Spacer [40.64 mm] 1.60 inch (QSK60 industrial)</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4918615</td><td>Spacer [52.07 mm] 2.05 inch (QSK38 marine and QSK50 industrial)</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4918600</td><td>Mounting plate</td><td>1</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4918602</td><td>Winch (cable included)</td><td>1</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>3644471</td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (M10 - 1.5 x 210, Class 9.8)</td><td>4</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3036230\">3036230</a></td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (M10 - 1.5 x 20, Class 9.8)</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3009503</td><td>Hexagon Nut</td><td>3</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3009330\">3009330</a></td><td>Plain washer</td><td>3</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3900623\">3900623</a></td><td>Hexagon head capscrew (M10 - 1.5 x 25, Class 9.8)</td><td>3</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>4918666</td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (3/8 x 16 x 8-1/2, Grade 8)</td><td>4</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>69102</td><td>Hexagon flange head capscrew (3/8 x 16 x 6-3/4, Grade 5)</td><td>4</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3013222\">3013222</a></td><td>Hexagon head capscrew (QSK50)</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>5299011</td><td>Spacer</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>5299012</td><td>Spacer</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>5299013</td><td>Hexagon head capscrew (QSK60)</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4918662</td><td>Winch drive adapter</td><td>1</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400237":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Rear Crankshaft Oil Seal Installer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the Rear Crankshaft Oil Seal Installer Kit, Part Number 4918762. The kit is used to remove and install the rear oil seal and rear wear sleeve oil seals on the crankshaft of the QST30 series engine with wet flywheel housings. For additional information, refer to Procedure 001-024 in the QST30 Series Engine Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021539\">4021539</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00244.png\" alt=\"22a00244.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Rear Crankshaft Oil Seal Installer Kit, Part Number 4918762</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918752</td><td>Spacer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163828</td><td>Capscrew</td><td>25</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with the Rear Crankshaft Oil Seal Installer Kit, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3825195</td><td>Rear Crankshaft Oil Seal/Wear Sleeve Removal and Installation Tool Kit</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400248":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Sensor Adapter</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Sensor Adapter, Part Number 4918864. The adapter is used on the oil pressure and temperature combination sensor on ISX engines which were manufactured from 1998 to 2002, without EGR. The adapter will create a clearance between the sensor probe and the oil gallery wall. This will prevent damage to the oil pressure and temperature sensor.</p><p>For additional information on the sensor adapter, refer to Procedure 019-155 (Oil Pressure/Temperature Sensor) Section 19 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Electronic Control System, Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin 3666259.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00327.png\" alt=\"22c00327.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Sensor Adapter, Part Number 4918864</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Shown above</td><td>4918864</td><td>Adapter</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400259":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Cylinder Block Inspection Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Cylinder Block Inspection Gauge, Part Number 4918968. An engineering design change to the QSK45 and QSK60 engines altered the design of the connecting rod from angle split to a straight split design. Due to this change, the cylinder blocks of engines already in service require internal machining to accept the new connecting rod. The gauge is to be used <b>only</b> for the side wall clearance of each cylinder location of the cylinder block, to determine if the required machining has been completed to the required specification.</p><p>For additional information, refer to Service Bulletin 4022147 on the QSK45, QSK60, QSK45G, QSK60G Cylinder Block Machining Procedure To Upgrade To Straight Split Connecting Rod.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600441.png\" alt=\"22600441.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Inspection Gauge, Part Number 4918968</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Shown above</td><td>4918968</td><td>Inspection gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400269":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Piston Assembly Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Piston Assembly Replacer Kit, Part Number 4919227. The kit is used to remove and install the piston and liner assembly in the QSK45 and QSK60 engines due to a design change of the connecting rod from an angle split to a horizontal split.</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-045-tr\">For additional information, refer to Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin 4021530</a></li><li>For additional information, refer to Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK45G and QSK60G Industrial Series Engines, Bulletin 4021383</li><li>For additional information, refer to Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK60G Generator CM700, Bulletin 4021396.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600457.png\" alt=\"22600457.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Piston Assembly Replacer Kit, Part Number 4919227. Items can be purchased separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918985</td><td>Cylinder liner replacer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918986</td><td>Replacer fixture</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4919120</td><td>Cylinder liner remover</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items included with the Replacer Fixture, can be purchased separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4918939</td><td>Replacer housing</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400279":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Data Link Cable</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Data Link Cable, Part Number 4919098. The cable connects to the Private J1939 Communication Network via 3-Pin connector off the ECM harness.</p><p>The cable is used on electronically controlled engines and will allow datalink adapters <b>not</b> manufactured by Cummins Inc. to connect to the 3-pin connector which was previously <b>not</b> possible. The cable acts as an adapter to transform the 3-pin connection to resemble a dash 9-pin Deutsch™ connection.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00339.png\" alt=\"22d00339.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Data Link Cable, Part Number 4919098</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919098</td><td>Data link cable</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Other Optional Items</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3163096</td><td>J1939 backbone cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3163597</td><td>J1939 adapter cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3162849</td><td>Power supply cable, cigar lighter adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3164653</td><td>4-pin Deutsch™ ECM power adapter harness</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400284":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Particulate Filter Cleaner</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052. The cleaner is used to Level 1 clean an ash loaded Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) from the ISB, QSB, ISC, ISL, QSL, ISM, ISX, and QSX engines. The cleaner is <b>not</b> designed to clean soot loaded DPFs. The cleaner requires 8.5 bar [120 psi] minimum shop air and 110 VAC 60 HZ electrical power. Adapter kits required to attach the DPF (sold separately) are shown in Table 4. A software unlock programmed card is required and sold separately, but is also included in the ISC, ISL, ISM, ISX,and adapter kit. Replacement filters available for the cleaner, and sold separately, are shown in Tables 2 and 3. Refer to the manufacturer&#x27;s user manual for appropriate cleaning procedures. Use the following procedures for additional information on the Aftertreatment Diesel Particulate Filter.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/101-011-041-tr\">Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the ISM, ISMe, and QSM11 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666322\">3666322</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/101-011-041-tr\">Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the ISC and ISL CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021569. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the ISB CM2100 and CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021578. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>For the Tier 4i QSB, use the following procedure in the QSB6.7 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022255. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>For the Tier 4i QSL, use the following procedure in the QSL9 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022256. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the ISX15 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022250. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the ISX11.9 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 2883445. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>For the Tier 4i QSX15, use the following procedure in the QSX15 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 2883557. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li><li>For the Tier 4i QSX11.9, use the following procedure in the QSX11.9 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 2883561. Refer to Procedure 011-041 in Section 11.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00330.png\" alt=\"22c00330.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Shown Above</td><td>4919052</td><td>Particulate filter cleaner</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00337.png\" alt=\"22c00337.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Replacement Air Filter Elements used with Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918896</td><td>Air filter element (oil separator)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4919053</td><td>Air filter element (canister filter)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4919054</td><td>Air filter element (HEPA filter)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4918851</td><td>Air filter element (water separator)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Replacement Air Filter used with Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4918841</td><td>Air filter (vacuum filter)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 4, Filter Cleaner Adapter Kits used with Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4918892</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (ISB)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4919172</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (ISC, ISL, ISM, and ISX) (Includes software unlock programmed card 4919055)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4919182</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (Retrofit)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4919790</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (Tier 4i QSB)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4919791</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (Tier 4i QSL)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4919792</td><td>Filter cleaner adapter kit (Tier 4i QSX)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 5, Programmed Card used with Particulate Filter Cleaner, Part Number 4919052</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919055</td><td>Programmed card (software unlock card)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 6, Replacement Rectangular Ring Seals and Threaded Plug kit</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892076</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for the upper adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919792, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892077</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for the lower adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919792, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919527</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for Part Number 4919182, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892078</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for upper adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919791, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892079</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for lower adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919791, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892080</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for upper adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919790, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892081</td><td>Rectangular ring seal (replacement gasket for lower adapter from Kit, Part Number 4919790, mounting adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919569</td><td>Threaded plug kit (for use on a DPF with Delta-P and Delta-T sensor boss connections)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400286":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Injector Protrusion Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Injector Protrusion Gauge, Part Number 4919196. The gauge is used to measure the injector protrusion of the K19, K38, and K50 engines, so the appropriate wear sleeve can be installed. The gauge is used with Depth Gauge Assembly, Part Number 3164438, or equivalent to eliminate measurement variation when using standard fuel injectors and wear sleeves.</p><p>For additional information see the following publications.</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/18-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) in Section 2 of the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021499</a></li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) in Section 2 of the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021528.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400293.png\" alt=\"22400293.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Injector Protrusion Gauge, Part Number 4919196</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919196</td><td>Injector protrusion gauge</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Used with Depth Gauge Assembly (Ordered Separately)</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3164438</td><td>Depth gauge assembly</td><td>N/A</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400291":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Turbocharger Actuator Inspection Gauge Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Turbocharger Actuator Inspection Gauge Kit, Part Number 4919281. The kit will identify if a variable geometry turbocharger has full travel of the variable geometry mechanism and will prevent unnecessary replacement of a turbocharger for the ISB, ISBe4 (4 Cylinder), ISBe4 (6 Cylinder), QSB6.7, QSB4.5, ISL, ISLe3, QSL9, 6C, C8.3, ISC, ISM, ISMe, QSM11, Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 engines. For additional information see the following publications.</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/10-010-134\">Refer to Procedure 010-134 (Variable Geometry Turbocharger Actuator, Electric) in Section 10 in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin 3666239.</a></li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/35-010-134\">Refer to Procedure 010-134 (Variable Geometry Turbocharger Actuator, Electric) in Section 10 in the ISM, ISMe, and QSM11 Service Manual, Bulletin 3666322.</a></li><li>Refer to Procedure 010-134 (Variable Geometry Turbocharger Actuator, Electric) in Section 10 in ISB CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021578.</li><li>Refer to Procedure 010-134 (Variable Geometry Turbocharger Actuator, Electric) in Section 10 in ISC and ISL CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021569.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00311.png\" alt=\"22d00311.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Turbocharger Actuator Inspection Gauge Kit, Part Number 4919281</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Turbocharger actuator inspection gauge, HE300Ve (ISB)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Turbocharger actuator inspection gauge, HE400Ve (ISC, ISL, and ISM)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Turbocharger actuator inspection gauge, HE500Ve (ISM and ISX)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400294":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Fuel Pump Gear Remover Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Fuel Pump Gear Remover Kit, Part Number 4919304. The kit is used to remove the drive gear and hub assembly on the QST 30 engine.</p><p>For additional information on removing the fuel pump gear, refer to Procedure 009-011 in Section 9 of the QST30 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021539\">4021539</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200473.png\" alt=\"22200473.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Fuel Pump Gear Remover Kit, Part Number 4919304</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919106</td><td>Hydraulic Cylinder</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4919517</td><td>Adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4919305</td><td>Mounting Plate</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4919307</td><td>Remover Screw</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094937\">3094937</a></td><td>Regular Hexagon Nut</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Remove the existing adapter from the hydraulic cylinder, Part Number 4919106.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00163.png\" alt=\"22a00163.png\"></figure><p>Install the adapter and o-ring assembly, Part Number 4919517 into the hydraulic cylinder until the assembly is fully inserted.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00165.png\" alt=\"22a00165.png\"></figure>","3400304":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Main Bearing Cap Remover</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for main bearing cap remover, Part Number 4919744. The remover is used to remove the main bearing caps in the K38, K50, QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines. For additional information, reference the following procedures.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK45G and QSK60G Industrial Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021383. Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK60G Generator CM700 Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021396. Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-001-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the KTA38GC CM558 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021642. Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</li><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK78 Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727. Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600465.png\" alt=\"22600465.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Main Bearing Cap Remover, Part Number 4919744</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919749</td><td>Main bearing cap remover</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4919466</td><td>Remover fixture</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4919468</td><td>Coupling nut</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4919469</td><td>Thrust washer</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400314":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Exhaust Lockplate Installer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Exhaust Lockplate Installer Kit, Part Number 4919376. The kit is used to install exhaust manifold capscrew lockplates to the required specification on the QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><p><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-011-007-tr\">For additional information, refer to Procedure 011-007 (Exhaust Manifold, Dry) in Section 11 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin 4021530.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00331.png\" alt=\"22d00331.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, QSK45 and QSK60 Lockplate Installer Kit, Part Number 4919376, Items can be Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919377</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4919378</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4919379</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, K38 and K50 Lockplate Installer Kit, Part Number 3163500, Items can be Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3162841</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3162842</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3162843</td><td>Lockplate installer</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400337":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Multi Module Switch Harness Assembly</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>The multiple ECM Bench Calibration Harness, Part Number 4919022, is to be attached permanently to the appropriate bench calibration harness for the QSK38, QSK50, and QSK60 CM850 and CM2150 engines. The multiple module switch box harness, Part Number 4918894, can be disconnected and used on other ROM boot harnesses that have been fitted with bench calibration harness pigtail, Part Number 4919022, which can be purchased separately.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00385.png\" alt=\"22d00385.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Multiple ECM Bench Calibration Harness, Part Number 4919064</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4918894</td><td>Switchable bench calibration harness</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4919022</td><td>Bench calibration harness pigtail</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Purpose</h3><p>Assembly of Multiple Module Harness</p><p>Insert the wire terminals from the multiple module harness, Part Number 4919022, into the connector cavity until they are fully seated on the bench calibration harness OEM connector. See Table 2.</p><p>Pull on the wire and make certain the pin is locked into the cavity.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Pin and Wire Locations</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bench Calibration Harness Part Number</td><td>3164185</td><td>4918583</td></tr><tr><td>White wire location</td><td>Pin 7</td><td>Pin 18</td></tr><tr><td>Yellow wire location</td><td>Pin 8</td><td>Pin 7</td></tr><tr><td>Gray wire location</td><td>Pin 12</td><td>Pin 8</td></tr><tr><td>Red wire location</td><td>Pin 34</td><td>Pin 41</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19601262.png\" alt=\"19601262.png\"></figure><p>Strain relieve the connection by installing a wire tie through the retainer clip attached to the 4-pin connector. This will secure the switch harness pigtail to the ROM boot harness.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19601263.png\" alt=\"19601263.png\"></figure><p>Install the multiple module switch box harness, Part Number 4918894, into the multiple module harness, Part Number 4919022.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19601264.png\" alt=\"19601264.png\"></figure>","3400361":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Charge Air Cooler Leak Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for charge air cooler leak test kit, Part Number 4919085. The kit is used to determine if the charge air cooler (CAC) needs to be repaired or replaced for all engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00388.png\" alt=\"22c00388.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Charge Air Cooler Leak Test Kit, Part Number 4919085</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3395943</td><td>Clamp, Spring Hose</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3926701</td><td>Clamp, Spring Hose</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3926702</td><td>Clamp, Spring Hose</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3926703\">3926703</a></td><td>Clamp, Spring Hose</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3926704\">3926704</a></td><td>Clamp, Spring Hose</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4919086</td><td>Gauge, Pressure</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4919124</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4919125</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>4919126</td><td>Cap, Leak Test</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>4919128</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>4919129</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>4919130</td><td>Cap, Leak Test</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>4919135</td><td>Cap, Leak Test</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>4919136</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>4919137</td><td>Cap, Leak Test</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>4919138</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>4919140</td><td>Chain, Retaining</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not Shown</b></td><td>4919739</td><td>Case, Storage</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Disconnect all tubes and hoses from the CAC inlet and outlet.</p><p>Install the appropriate flexible hoses, included in kit, Part Number 4919085, onto the CAC.</p><p>Install the appropriate spring hose clamps included in kit, Part Number 4919085 and tighten.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>8 n•m [71 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00501.png\" alt=\"10c00501.png\"></figure><p>Install the appropriate leak test caps into the hoses.</p><p>Install the appropriate spring hose clamps included in kit, Part Number 4919085 and tighten.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>8 n•m [71 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00502.png\" alt=\"10c00502.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Equipment damage and personal injury can result from unrestrained leak test caps blowing out of the hoses. Be certain the plugs are properly restrained.</p></div></div><p>Install the leak test cap retaining chains in front of the CAC in such a way as to limit the movement of each cap, in case the cap blows out of the hose when air pressure is applied. The chains <b>must</b> limit the caps to the shortest possible movement.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00503.png\" alt=\"10c00503.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Excessive air pressure can blow a leak test cap out of a hose, resulting in equipment damage or personal injury. Do NOT use more than 241 kPa [35 psi] air pressure.</p></div></div><p>Connect the flexible hose to the quick connect fitting on the leak test cap.</p><p>Connect the pressure gauge assembly to the flexible hose.</p><p>The safety relief valve on the leak test cap will relieve pressure at 276 kPa [40 psi]. If escaping air is heard, it is an indication that the maximum test air pressure has been exceeded.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00504.png\" alt=\"10c00504.png\"></figure><p>Use shop air to pressurize the CAC while watching the pressure gauge readout. Do <b>not</b> exceed 241 kPa [35 psi].</p><p>When the pressure drops to 207 kPa [30 psi], begin timing with a stop watch.</p><p>If the pressure drop is greater than 49 kPa [7 psi] in 15 seconds, the CAC <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/oi100sn.png\" alt=\"oi100sn.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Once the test is completed, relieve the pressure in the CAC by disconnecting the flexible hose from the quick connect fitting on the leak test cap.</p></div></div><p>Disconnect the gauge assembly and flexible hose from the leak test cap.</p><p>Remove the leak test components from the CAC.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Periodically check the relief valve on the leak test caps to ensure that they start passing air at 276 Pa [40 psi].</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10c00505.png\" alt=\"10c00505.png\"></figure>","3400362":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 4919752. The kit is used to remove and install the crankshaft rear oil seal on the V28, K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50 engines.</p><p>Use the following procedure for additional information on the crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 4919752, in the K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50 Engines Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-001-024-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-024 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22s00001.png\" alt=\"22s00001.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 4919752</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892125</td><td>Installer, crankshaft seal</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892128</td><td>Nut, hexagon flange</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3018007\">3018007</a></td><td>Washer, plain</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3331123</td><td>Screw, socket head cap</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4918855</td><td>Screw, hexagon head cap</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4919753</td><td>Remover, seal</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4919756</td><td>Adapter, mounting (V28)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4919757</td><td>Adapter, mounting (K38, K50, QSK38, QSK50)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>4919759</td><td>Screw, self tapping metal</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>4919771</td><td>Pilot, crankshaft seal</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400372":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Electrical Power Supply Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for electrical power supply kits, Part Number 2892089 and 2892090. The kits are used with the appropriate Cummins® bench calibration cables to allow the electronic control module (ECM) to be calibrated prior to being installed on the engine. The appropriate kit (or equivalent power source) is required when calibrating a CM2250 ECM, however, the kits can also be used with all Cummins® bench calibration cables. Service Tool Instruction, Bulletin Number 3377791, contains additional information regarding available bench calibration cables and their use.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22d00431.png\" alt=\"22d00431.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Electrical Power Supply Kit (120 Volt, 60 Hz), Part Number 2892089</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892082</td><td>Electrical power supply (input: 120-VAC, 60 Hz, 5.5 Amp; output: 13.8-VDC, 23 Amp; includes power cable with NEMA 5-15 plug)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892084</td><td>Electrical power cable (1.83 m [6 ft], includes 10 Ampere Time Delay Fuse)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Electrical Power Supply Kit (230 Volt, 50 Hz), Part Number 2892090</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892083</td><td>Electrical power supply (input: 230-VAC, 50 Hz; output: 13.8-VDC, 23 Amp; includes power cable with European &quot;Schuko&quot; plug)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892084</td><td>Electrical power cable (1.83 m [6 ft], includes 10 Ampere Time Delay Fuse)</td></tr><tr><td>Optional item <b>not</b> Shown</td><td>2892085</td><td>Electrical power cable with BS 1363 Plug (For use in the United Kingdom, use <b>only</b> with kit, Part Number 2892090).</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Replacement Parts for Electrical Power Supply Kits, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td><b>not</b> shown</td><td>2892086</td><td>Fuse, 6.3 Amp, GDC-6.3A, (power supply internal fuse, use with kit, Part Number 2892090)</td></tr><tr><td><b>not</b> shown</td><td>2892087</td><td>Fuse, 4.0 Amp, GDC-4A, (power supply internal fuse, use with kit, Part Number 2892089)</td></tr><tr><td><b>not</b> shown</td><td>2892088</td><td>Fuse, 10 Amp, time delay, (use with output power cable, Part Number 2892084)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400381":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Fuel System Leak Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for fuel system leak test kit, Part Number 2892246. The kit is used to test the injectors on the QSK19 MCRS engines.</p><p>Use the following procedure in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021592\">4021592</a>, for additional information on the fuel system leak test kit. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-006-026-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-026 in Section 6.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22k00003.png\" alt=\"22k00003.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Fuel System Leak Test Kit, Part Number 2892246</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892247</td><td>Adapter, Leak Test</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892248</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2892296</td><td>Hose, Flexible</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2892297</td><td>Adapter, Leak Test</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678610\">3678610</a></td><td>Plug, Threaded</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3963990\">3963990</a></td><td>Washer, Sealing</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4098549\">4098549</a></td><td>Washer, Sealing</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>3164614</td><td>Tester, Fuel Pump</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not shown</td><td>2892397</td><td>Case, Storage</td><td>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400383":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Thermostat Seal Installer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for thermostat seal installer, Part Number 2892254. The installer is used to install the thermostat seal to the correct depth.</p><p>Use the following procedures for additional information on the thermostat seal installer.</p><ul><li>Refer to Procedure 008-016 in Section 8 in the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-016\">Refer to Procedure 008-016 in Section 8 in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021530.</a></li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-008-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-013 in Section 8 in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021528.</a></li><li>Refer to Procedure 008-016 in Section 8 in the QSK78 Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22k00001.png\" alt=\"22k00001.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Thermostat Seal Installer, Part Number 2892254</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3822979</td><td>Handle</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892255</td><td>Installer plate</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400386":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Injector Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for injector test kit, Part Number 2892293. The kit is used to test all Modular Common Rail System (MCRS) injectors to determine if the solenoid is functioning properly.</p><p>Use the following procedures for instructions on use of the Injector Test Kit.</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-006-026-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-026 in Section 6 in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin 4021592.</a></li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-006-026-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-026 in Section 6 in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021528.</a></li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-006-026-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-026 in Section 6 in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021530.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22e00042.png\" alt=\"22e00042.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Injector Test Kit, Part Number 2892293</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892294</td><td>Injector tester</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892295</td><td>Electrical wiring harness</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>2892302</td><td>Storage Case</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400392":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Leak Test Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Leak Test Kit, Part Number 2892320, used to detect leaks in all engine fluid systems (lubrication, coolant, and fuel) using a cordless “True UV” light that will detect the presence of fluorescent dye additive. The kit is also capable of detecting leaks in air conditioning systems, using the appropriate dye.</p><p>Leak Test Kit, Part Number 2892320, will replace all previous leak test kits and black light kits.</p><p>Reference the appropriate service manual for the recommended test procedure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000080.png\" alt=\"22000080.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Leak Test Kit, Part Number 2892320</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892355</td><td>Battery Charger (12-VDC - 24-VDC)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892352</td><td>Battery Charger (100-VAC - 240-VAC, 50-60 Hz w/adapters)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2892358</td><td>Protective Glasses (UV Absorbing, Clear)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2892319</td><td>Battery (Stick Type)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400399":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Radiator Cap Adapter</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for various radiator cap adapters that are used with Coolant System Tester Kit, Part Number 3824319. Reference the descriptions in Table 1 to select the correct adapter for the appropriate radiator.</p><p>Reference the appropriate service manual for the recommended test procedure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000078.png\" alt=\"22000078.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Radiator Cap Adapters</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164211</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Navistar (1996 or newer), Part Number 2039390C1, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3824313</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Volvo®, Part Number 1542591, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824311</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Mack™, Part Number 5516031410, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824314</td><td>Adapter (Truck (B) size to quick coupler)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824315</td><td>Adapter (High flow standard automotive size cam lock adapter)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824316</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Western Star, Part Number 200009-0002, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824317</td><td>Adapter (Transit Bus adapter)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824318</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Volvo®, Part Number 6794968, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>3824430</td><td>Adapter (Mount on top of coolant system tester to test pop-off pressure or Truck (B) size cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919772</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Volvo®, VN series Part Number 1674922, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919773</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Ford® E-350 International 7.3L, Part Number(s) RS-103, F6DZ-8100A, 12R-16, and 31406, radiator cap(s))</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919774</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Kenworth™, Part Number N5349001, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919775</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Volvo® VN series 2006 and newer, Part Number 20519046, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919776</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Freightliner® Columbia 2008, Part Number(s) N9685001 or BHTN9685001, radiator cap(s))</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Not Shown</td><td>4919777</td><td>Adapter (Fits radiators using Freightliner® Columbia, Part Number 05-20763-000, radiator cap)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400408":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Expansion Plug Installer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for expansion plug installer, Part Number 2892394. The tool is used to install the expansion plugs, to the correct depth, into the fuel pump for the QSK19, QSK38, QSK50, and QSK60 MCRS engines.</p><p>Use the following procedures for additional information on the expansion plug installer.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021592\">4021592</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22500001.png\" alt=\"22500001.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Expansion Plug Installer, Part Number 2892394</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892394</td><td>Expansion plug installer</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400409":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Expansion Plug Remover Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for expansion plug remover kit, Part Number 2892440. The kit is used in conjunction with a 3/4-16 slide hammer assembly, Cummins® Part Number 2892442 or equivalent, to remove the expansion plugs from the fuel pump for the QSK19, QSK38, QSK50, and QSK60 MCRS engines</p><p>Use the following procedures for additional information on the expansion plug installer.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021592\">4021592</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22500003.png\" alt=\"22500003.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Expansion Plug Remover Kit, Part Number 2892440</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>4919742</td><td>Collet</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4919743</td><td>Collet expander</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400410":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Coolant Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for coolant replacer kit, Part Number 2892459. The kit is used to drain and fill the engine coolant for all Cummins® engines.</p><p>Use the following procedures for more information on the operation of the coolant replacer kit.</p><ul><li>For the ISX15 CM2250, use the following procedure in the ISX15 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022250. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15, use the following procedure in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/10-008-018-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</a></li><li>For the ISM, ISMe, and QSM11, use the following procedure in the ISM, ISMe, and QSM11 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666322\">3666322</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/35-008-018-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</a></li><li>For the ISB CM2100 and CM2150, use the following procedure in the ISB CM2100 and CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021578. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the ISB6.7 CM2250, use the following procedure in the ISB6.7 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022254. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the ISC and ISL CM2150, use the following procedure in the ISC and ISL CM2150 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021569. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the ISC8.3 and ISL9 CM2250, use the following procedure in the ISC8.3 and ISL9 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022257. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the ISB, ISBe, ISBe4, QSB4.5, QSB5.9, and QSB6.7 (Common Rail Fuel System), use the following procedure in the ISB, ISBe, ISBe4, QSB4.5, QSB5.9, and QSB6.7 (Common Rail Fuel System) Service Manual, Bulletin 4021271. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the QSL9 CM2250, use the following procedure in the QSL9 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022256. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li><li>For the QSB6.7 CM2250, use the following procedure in the QSB6.7 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022255. Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000088.png\" alt=\"22000088.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Coolant Replacer Kit, Part Number 2892459 Table 1 - The following items (shown) are available for individual sale</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892474</td><td>Connector, Quick Disconnect (1/4” NPTF)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892475</td><td>Connector, Quick Disconnect (3/8” NPTF)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2 - The following additional items (not shown) are available for individual sale</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>2892479</td><td>Tank, Storage</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>5296521</td><td>Seal, O-Ring (Replacement for coolant replacer access cap)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","3400418":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Counterbore Cutter Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for counterbore cutter kit, Part Number 2892436. The kit is used with counterbore cutter driver, Part Number 3163785 to cut the cylinder block liner counterbore on the Signature™, ISX, ISX15, and QSX15 engines.</p><p>Use the following procedures for more information on the operation of the counterbore cutter kit.</p><ul><li>For the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15, use the following procedure in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. Refer to Procedure 001-058 in Section 1.</li><li>For the ISX15 CM2250, use the following procedure in the ISX15 CM2250 Service Manual, Bulletin 4022250. Refer to Procedure 001-058 in Section 1.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22o00007.png\" alt=\"22o00007.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Counterbore Cutter Kit, Part Number 2892436 Table 1 - The following items (shown) are available for individual sale</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892423</td><td>Plate, mounting</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892460</td><td>Gauge, locating</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2892463</td><td>Screw, hexagon head cap</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4919026</td><td>Washer, thrust</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>5296502</td><td>Point, gauge contact</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>5296505</td><td>Gauge, feeler</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>5296519</td><td>Plug, cylinder bore (used in 150 mm cylinder block bore)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>5296520</td><td>Plug, cylinder bore (used in 152 mm cylinder block bore)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>5296529</td><td>Insert, cutter bit</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>5296531</td><td>Bit, cutter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>5296533</td><td>Plate, cutter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>5296543</td><td>Plug, protective</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2 - The following additional items (<b>not</b> shown) are available for individual sale</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>2892402</td><td>Cylinder liner shim - 0.51 mm [.020 in ]</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>2892403</td><td>Cylinder liner shim - 0.81 mm [.032 in]</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>5296530</td><td>Cutter bit screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>5296534</td><td>Cutter bit wrench (T8-Torx™)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","3400419":"<h3>Description</h3><p>INLINE™ 6 Data Link Adapter Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the INLINE™ 6 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 2892092, and the associated cables to connect a personal computer to the data link adapter. The INLINE™ 6 data link adapter is designed for use with the SAE J1708 and J1939 standard protocols. The INLINE™ 6 data link adapter is used with software applications such as INSITE™ Electronic Service Tool 7.5 and later versions. The INLINE™ 6 supports all Cummins Inc. electronic engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22100120.png\" alt=\"22100120.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, INLINE™ 6 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 2892092</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2892093</td><td>INLINE™ 6 data link adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2892176</td><td>USB cable, (4.3 m [14 feet])</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163096</td><td>J1939 backbone adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3163597</td><td>J1939 gender change adapter</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4919780</td><td>Data link cable (DB25F 9-Pin Deutsch™ connector)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>4918713</td><td>Storage case</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2892095</td><td>INLINE™ 6 software compact disc</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>2892096</td><td>INLINE™ 6 ruggedized protective boot</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>3165141</td><td>DB25F/2-pin Weather-Pack™/2-pin Weather-Pack™/3-pin Deutsch™ cable</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Items Used with INLINE™ 6 Data Link Adapter Kit, Part Number 2892092, Purchased Separately</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>4919797</td><td>DB25F/3-pin Deutsch™/3-pin Deutsch™/2-pin Weather-Pack™ cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>3824440</td><td>DB25F 8-Pin AMP™ connector</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>4918418</td><td>DB9F-DB9M serial cable</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>3165160</td><td>DB25F/6-pin Deutsch™ cable</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000084.png\" alt=\"22000084.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>A fully populated USB cable, Part Number 2892176, or DB9F-DB9M, serial cable, Part Number 4918418, <b>must</b> be used.</p></div></div><p>Connect the DB9F-DB9M serial cable, Part Number 4918418, or the USB cable, Part Number 2892176 to the RS-232 serial port or the USB port of the computer and to the INLINE™ 6 data link adapter, Part Number 2892093.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000085.png\" alt=\"22000085.png\"></figure><p>The INLINE™ 6 data link adapter requires +8-VDC to +50-VDC at 250mA that can be supplied through the OEM connector or by a separate power source.</p><p>Connect the appropriate data link cable to the INLINE™ 6 data link adapter, Part Number 2892093.</p><p>With the data link cable connected to the INLINE™ 6 data link adapter, connect the other end of the data link cable to the vehicle cab or engine compartment data link connector.</p><p>Launch the electronic service tool application software.</p><p>The following are the INLINE™ 6 Adapter Indicator Lamp Functions:</p><h4>Power Lamp</h4><ul><li>When the power lamp is lighted green continuously, this means DC power is being supplied to the adapter at the proper voltage level. The INLINE™ 6 adapter requires +8-VDC to +50-VDC at 250 mA that can be supplied through the OEM connector or by a separate power source.</li><li>When the power lamp is lighted red continuously, this means that either the INLINE™ 6 adapter is receiving a low power supply voltage (less than 8-VDC) or is <b>only</b> receiving power from the USB port.</li><li>When the power lamp is off, this means that the INLINE™ 6 is receiving no power.</li></ul><h4>CAN 1 Port Lamp</h4><ul><li>A CAN 1 red flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is physically connected to a CAN data link. However, it is <b>not</b> communicating with an ECM on the CAN data link. A CAN 1 green flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is communicating with an ECM on the CAN data link.</li></ul><h4>CAN 2 Port Lamp</h4><ul><li>A CAN 2 red flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is physically connected to a CAN data link. However, it is <b>not</b> communicating with an ECM on the CAN data link. A CAN 2 green flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is communicating with an ECM on the CAN data link.</li></ul><h4>J1708 Port Lamp</h4><ul><li>A J1708 red flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is physically connected to a J1708 data link. However, it is <b>not</b> communicating with an ECM on the J1708 data link. A J1708 green flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is communicating with an ECM on the J1708 data link.</li></ul><h4>RS‐232 Port Lamp</h4><ul><li>An RS-232 green flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is connected to an active RS-232 port and exchanging communications. An RS-232 lamp in the OFF state indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is <b>not</b> communicating over the RS-232 port.</li></ul><h4>USB Port Lamp</h4><ul><li>A USB green flashing lamp indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is connected to an active USB port and is exchanging communications. A USB lamp in the OFF state indicates that the INLINE™ 6 adapter is <b>not</b> communicating over the USB port.</li></ul><h3>Document History</h3>","3400422":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Inspection Gauge</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for inspection gauge, Part Number 5298508. The gauge is used to check the cylinder head valve guide bore for distortion, and used with valve guide reamer, Part Number 5298510, for repair of QSK19, QSK45, and QSK60 engines.</p><ul><li>For the QSK19, use the following procedure for additional information on the valve guide inspection gauge in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021592\">4021592</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li><li>For the QSK45, QSK60, QSK60 CM850 MCRS and QSK60 CM2150 MCRS, use the following procedure for additional information on the valve guide inspection gauge in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600397.png\" alt=\"22600397.png\"></figure><p>Inspection Gauge, Part Number 5298508</p><h3>Document History</h3>","3400423":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Valve Guide Reamer</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the valve guide reamer, Part Number 5298510. The reamer is used, with inspection gauge, Part Number 5298508, to machine the valve guide bore of the cylinder head of QSK19, QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This reamer is <b>not</b> to be used on QSK60 Gas engine cylinder heads.</p></div></div><ul><li>For the QSK19, use the following procedure for additional information on the valve guide reamer in the QSK19, QSK19 CM850 MCRS, and QSK19 CM2150 MCRS Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021592\">4021592</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/20-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li><li>For the QSK 45, QSK60, QSK60 CM850 MCRS and QSK60 CM2150 MCRS, use the following procedure for additional information on the valve guide reamer in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22k00007.png\" alt=\"22k00007.png\"></figure><p>Valve Guide Reamer, Part Number 5298510</p><h3>Document History</h3>","3400432":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for rear crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 5298540. The kit is used to remove and install the QSK23 rear crankshaft oil seal (with or without wear sleeve).</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure for additional information on the seal replacer in the QSK23 Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021375\">4021375</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/89-001-024\">Refer to Procedure 001-024 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22h00001.png\" alt=\"22h00001.png\"></figure><p>Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298540</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, The following items are available for individual sale.</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3164967</td><td>Replacer Screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3065497\">3065497</a></td><td>Hexagon Head Cap Screw</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3164218</td><td>Drill</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> Shown</td><td>5298543</td><td>Self Tapping Metal Screw</td><td>36</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","3400458":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Water Pump Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Water Pump Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298838. The kit is used to replace the oil and water seals on the QSK23 engine water pump. The kit components are assembled together when installing the engine water pump oil seal. For the engine water pump water seal, <b>only</b> the handle component is used.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure for additional information on the seal installer in the QSK23 Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021375\">4021375</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/89-008-062-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-062 in section 8.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22h00003.png\" alt=\"22h00003.png\"></figure><p>Water Pump Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298838</p><h3>Document History</h3>","3400461":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for the Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298874. The kit is used to replace the engine crankshaft front oil seal and wear sleeve on K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 series diesel and natural gas engines.</p><p>For additional information on the use of Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298874, use the following procedure in the appropriate engine service manual.</p><ul><li>Use the following procedure in the K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-001-023-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-023 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Use the following procedure in the KTA38GC CM558 Service Manual, Bulletin 4021642. Refer to Procedure 001-023 in Section 1.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22s00008.png\" alt=\"22s00008.png\"></figure><p>Crankshaft Seal Replacer Kit, Part Number 5298874</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1: The following items are available for individual sale.</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3163695</td><td>Screw, Hexagon Head Cap</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163764</td><td>Screw, Drilling</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3163765</td><td>Screw, Forcing</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>3824764</td><td>Sleeve, Protective</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>5298877</td><td>Expander, Wear Sleeve</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>S-640</td><td>Washer, Plain</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","3400474":"<h3>Description</h3><p>Service Tool Component Kit</p><h3>Purpose</h3><p>This document provides information for Service Tool Component Kit, Part Number 5299014. The kit is used to upgrade existing fuel pump lifting fixture kit, Part Number 4918603, now obsolete and superseded by, Part Number 5299015, to have the same functionality as current fuel pump lifting fixture kit, Part Number 5299015, used to remove and install the fuel pump on the QSK50 MCRS and QSK60 MCRS engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22300007.png\" alt=\"22300007.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Service Tool Component Kit, Part Number 5299014</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reference Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td><td>Available to Purchase</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3013222\">3013222</a></td><td>Screw, Hexagon Head Cap</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>5299011</td><td>Spacer</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>5299012</td><td>Spacer</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>5299013</td><td>Screw, Hex Flange Head Cap</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb020001":"<h2>CENSE™ Phase 1.5 Harness Repair Instructions</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>It has recently been discovered that the all Phase 1.5 CENSE™ right-bank wiring harness, Part Number 4017464, on QSK60C engines have been produced incorrectly. The exhaust gas temperature connectors have been wired incorrectly for power cylinders 1, 2, 5, and 7, resulting in incorrect diagnosis of cylinder fault codes.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine Serial Numbers Affected (QSK60 Only)</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>33150763</td><td>33150602</td><td>33150387</td><td>33150015</td><td>33149343</td><td>33148906</td><td>33148449</td><td>33147903</td></tr><tr><td>33150758</td><td>33150598</td><td>33150374</td><td>33149988</td><td>33149314</td><td>33148901</td><td>33148444</td><td>33147878</td></tr><tr><td>33150755</td><td>33150596</td><td>33150363</td><td>33149973</td><td>33149277</td><td>33148897</td><td>33148401</td><td>33147584</td></tr><tr><td>33150710</td><td>33150591</td><td>33150345</td><td>33149964</td><td>33149264</td><td>33148890</td><td>33148390</td><td>33147332</td></tr><tr><td>33150706</td><td>33150587</td><td>33150341</td><td>33149951</td><td>33149258</td><td>33148781</td><td>33148385</td><td>33147260</td></tr><tr><td>33150695</td><td>33150585</td><td>33150337</td><td>33149934</td><td>33149252</td><td>33148684</td><td>33148377</td><td>33147083</td></tr><tr><td>33150687</td><td>33150580</td><td>33150331</td><td>33149903</td><td>33149247</td><td>33148620</td><td>33148355</td><td>33147075</td></tr><tr><td>33150674</td><td>33150576</td><td>33150321</td><td>33149719</td><td>33149204</td><td>33148616</td><td>33148304</td><td>33146876</td></tr><tr><td>33150668</td><td>33150573</td><td>33150313</td><td>33149702</td><td>33149201</td><td>33148608</td><td>33148280</td><td>33146847</td></tr><tr><td>33150666</td><td>33150568</td><td>33150305</td><td>33149688</td><td>33149159</td><td>33148601</td><td>33148259</td><td>33146819</td></tr><tr><td>33150657</td><td>33150563</td><td>33150291</td><td>33149640</td><td>33149077</td><td>33148591</td><td>33148244</td><td>33146809</td></tr><tr><td>33150651</td><td>33150561</td><td>33150270</td><td>33149493</td><td>33149075</td><td>33148586</td><td>33148215</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150649</td><td>33150557</td><td>33150262</td><td>33149471</td><td>33149029</td><td>33148539</td><td>33148196</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150645</td><td>33150522</td><td>33150189</td><td>33149461</td><td>33148968</td><td>33148534</td><td>33148182</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150635</td><td>33150518</td><td>33150181</td><td>33149421</td><td>33148962</td><td>33148528</td><td>33148170</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150625</td><td>33150420</td><td>33150169</td><td>33149408</td><td>33148954</td><td>33148467</td><td>33148122</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150619</td><td>33150407</td><td>33150147</td><td>33149359</td><td>33148948</td><td>33148463</td><td>33148077</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33150615</td><td>33150397</td><td>33150134</td><td>33149356</td><td>33148940</td><td>33148456</td><td>33148009</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Subsequent engines from and including ESN 33146793 were rectified in the manufacturing plant and therefore require no modification.</p></div></div><p>As a result, the temperature readings and fault codes obtained via the CENSE™ diagnostic software, INSITE™, do <b>not</b> correspond correctly to their associated power cylinders.</p><p>For example, INSITE™ can indicate low or high exhaust gas temperature from cylinder number 1 when it is actually measuring the exhaust gas from cylinder number 7. As a consequence, this would mislead a technician into disassembling a healthy power cylinder when investigating the cause of the fault code.</p><p>This is a confirmed issue with the Phase 1.5 CENSE™ harness; therefore, there is no requirement for any inspection or fault verification procedure.</p><p>The cause of this issue is through a wiring harness design error.</p><p>Mis-diagnosing power cylinder performance can lead an unhealthy power cylinder going undetected. This would obviously result in degradation in general engine performance and possible progressive component damage.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Due to un-serviceability of the right bank CENSE™ harness (in which the fault lies), the repair instructions instruct modification to the wiring within the CENSE™ ECM housing. Altering the wiring at this location essentially “cancels out” the mis-wire on the right bank harness.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/rearofengine.jpg.png\" alt=\"rearofengine.jpg.png\"></figure><p>Remove the six M6 capscrews.</p><p>Remove the CENSE™ housing cover.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>alankey.jpg.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/al/a/alankey.jpg.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><p>Remove the module upper connector with a 4-mm allen key as shown.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>plugdetach.jpg.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/pl/u/plugdetach.jpg.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><p>Using the Deutsch pin removal tool, Part Number 3824815, remove and reinsert the pins into their correct terminal. See table 1.</p><p>Label each wire when disconnected with the new pin location.</p><p>As each pin is reinserted, there will be a click as the terminal locks in the connector. Give the wire a gentle pull to ensure it is located.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Remove from Terminal</td><td>Reinsert into Terminal</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>01</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>01</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>04</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>22</td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>31</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>21</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>alankey.jpg.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/al/a/alankey.jpg.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><p>Reconnect the connector with the 4-mm allen key.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>3 n•m [27 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/rearofengine.jpg.png\" alt=\"rearofengine.jpg.png\"></figure><p>Refit the CENSE™ housing cover.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><p>After completing the rewire, plug the connector back into the CENSE™ ECM and test using CENSE™ INSITE™. Do this by going into the real time monitor feature, selecting all 16 EGT sensors. Disconnect the exhaust thermocouples from the wiring harness one at a time while observing the real time monitor display. Ensure that the correct cylinder temperature reading goes to “failed” as its associated sensor is disconnected. If everything is functioning correctly, move onto the next sensor.</p><p>Once satisfied that the CENSE™ system is functioning correctly, there is a need to identify that the CENSE™ wiring has been modified. This <b>must</b> be done by stamping the word “RW” (rewired) with letter stamps on the right hand side of the CENSE™ ECM housing.</p><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>19600198.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/19/6/19600198.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb020016":"<h2>Engine Lube Pump Suction Head to Housing Gasket</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>It has been found that on some QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines the torque on the capscrews that hold the engine lube pump suction head to the housing do <b>not</b> meet specifications. This early warning instructs the technicians to check the torque on these bolts, if the oil pan is being removed for another reason.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines.</p><p>Low or erratic oil pressure.</p><p>The capscrews that hold the engine lube pump suction head to the housing do <b>not</b> meet the 47 N•m [35 ft-lb] specification.</p><p>The gasket between the engine lube pump suction head and housing is crushing, and the capscrews are loosing some of their torque.</p><p>If the torque is complete lost, the engine lube pump could loose suction, causing a loss of engine oil pressure.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600502.png\" alt=\"07600502.png\"></figure><p>Torque the engine lube pump suction head to housing capscrews to specification.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>47 n•m [35 ft-lb]</p></div></div><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb040013":"<h2>Bench Calibration Harness Correction</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Warning is to provide information on how to repair the QST30 bench calibration harness, Part Number 3164458.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QST30.</p><p>The QST30 bench calibration harness, Part Number 3164458, was built without the necessary jumper wires required to function properly. This results in an inability to transfer calibrations to the ECM and can result in various fault codes.</p><p>All of the QST30 bench calibration harnesses, Part Number 3164458, initially exhibited this problem. <b>Only</b> those who have notified Service Products or Service Tools have received the repair components and instructions.</p><p>The initial bench calibration harnesses were built incorrectly. Since that time, QST30 bench calibration harnesses with ROM boot have been released. None of the QST30 bench calibration harnesses with ROM boot exhibit this problem.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>The necessary jumper wires and instructions for installing them are available by contacting Josh Thomas in Cummins Service Tools at (812) 377-1746.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb040034":"<h2>Loose Gear Cover Spacer Plate Capscrews</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Oil leaks reported coming from the 19 liter engines front gear cover spacer plate due to capscrews becoming loose from gasket relaxation.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>This applies to the K19, K19G, QSK19, and QSK19G engines.</p><p>Capscrews are becoming loose on the gear cover spacer plate.</p><p>None.</p><p>Gasket relaxation.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>When installing gear cover spacer plate capscrews:</p><ul><li>Install a hardened washer, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3042329\">3042329</a>, as illustrated in Figure 1. Each capscrew will now have two washers (Figure 1).</li><li>Then apply Loctite™ 271 thread-locker (10 mL [0.338 oz] bottle, Part Number 3824038, or 50 mL [1.69 oz] bottle, Part Number 3375068) to the capscrews, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3014766\">3014766</a>) in the method described below.</li></ul><div class=\"fig-missing\">Иллюстрация <code>e04034_01.jpg.png</code> не выгружена — <a href=\"https://quickserve.cummins.com/rtgraphics/english/service/e0/4/e04034_01.jpg.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">открыть на QuickServe ↗</a></div><p>Figure 1.</p><p>Apply three drops of Loctite™ 271 thread-locker (available as Cummins Inc. service tool part) to each capscrew starting 2 to 3 threads from the tip of the capscrew (12 capscrews on K19, 14 capscrews on QSK19 and QSK19G).</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>48 n•m [35 ft-lb]</p></div></div><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb060006":"<h2>Fan Hub Locknut</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Notification is to inform the field service locations of possible loose fan hub locknuts, Part Number 3171137, on QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSK45 and QSK60 engines built after 16-September-2005 with the following options:</p><ul><li>FA6165</li><li>FA6189</li><li>FA6190</li><li>FA6191</li><li>FA6196</li></ul><p>Could possibly experience fan hub vibrations leading to loosening of the fan belt pulley. Inspect for twists or cracks in the fan belt.</p><p>None.</p><p>Under investigation.</p><p>Loss of engine cooling capability and possible damage to the fan and radiator.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><ol><li>Order quantity one locknut, Part Number 3171137.</li><li>Remove grease over the original locknut.</li><li>Remove the installed locknut.</li><li>Remove the existing lock washer, Part Number 4000744, and discard.</li><li>Install the original locknut. Make sure that the original locknut has the chamfer facing away from the spacer washer (which can be seen right behind the locknut).</li><li>Torque the original locknut to 600 N•m [443 ft-lb].</li><li>Apply Loctite 648 to the second locknut.</li><li>Install the second locknut over the shaft with the chamfer facing towards the chamfer on the previously installed locknut.</li><li>Torque the second locknut to 250 N•m [184 ft-lb].</li><li>Make sure that approximately 300 cc of grease (Mineral oil grease CES20014) is filled into the cavity around the locknut before installing the cover.</li><li>Install the o-ring into the groove in the spacer mounting end cover and lightly lubricate the o-ring. The spacer can be pushed fully home into the fan hub before tightening the capscrews. Tighten the capscrews to 280 N•m [207 ft-lb].</li></ol><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb070004":"<h2>Possible Oil Leaks - Wet Flywheel Housings</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Field Notification is to inform the field of possible oil leaks from a threaded mounting hole on wet flywheel housings installed on QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSK45 Engines with Option FH 6047</p><p>QSK60 Engines with Option FH 6047</p><p>An oil leak at the second from the top, rear threaded hole, on the wet flywheel housing may be observed from the mounting pad on the left side of the flywheel housing.</p><p>None.</p><p>The threaded mounting hole was drilled too deep when the flywheel housing was machined.</p><p>Loss of performance, premature wear, or damage to components inside the wet flywheel housing.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><ol><li>Order quantity one, M20 X 2.5-6g threaded capscrew. Make sure the capscrew has at least 38 mm [1.5 in.] of thread.</li><li>Cut off the head of the capscrew so that the threaded half of the capscrew is between 25.4 mm [1 in.] and 32 mm [1.25 in.] long. Discard the head.</li><li>Grind a slot in the cut off end of the capscrew, such that it can be turned with a flat screwdriver.</li><li>Clean the threaded hole of the flywheel housing with brake cleaner, and dry with compressed air.</li><li>Apply a standard Stud Lock Loctite® to the remaining piece of the capscrew threads.</li><li>Install the remaining piece of the capscrew into the threaded hole of the flywheel housing until snug.</li></ol><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb070005":"<h2>Continuously Activated Fuel Lift Pumps</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Electronic fuel lift pumps on QST30 engines operate in the KEY ON position without the engine operating. Extended periods in this state can cause damage to and eventual failure of the fuel lift pump.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All QST30 engines equipped with electronic fuel lift pumps in industrial applications.</p><p>Engine will <b>not</b> start or registers low power, once the fuel lift pump fails.</p><p>Reference the No Start symptom tree.</p><p>If the lift pump is operating without a cooling fuel flow for more than 30 seconds, the brush and commutator within the pump will sustain damage and eventually fail.</p><p>If the fuel pump fails, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Do not have the engine in KEY ON position for more than 30 seconds without operating the engine. If the engine needs to be left in the KEY ON position for troubleshooting purposes, disconnect the fuel lift pump. Connect the fuel lift pump when the engine is ready for normal operation.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb070007":"<h2>Troubleshooting and Repair Direction for High Blowby and/or Oil Consumption</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>See Service Bulletin, High Blowby and Lubricating Oil Consumption Caused by Dirt and Dust Ingestion, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/5613318\">5613318</a>.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><h3>Resolution</h3><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb070015":"<h2>Engine Will Not Start</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This early field notification informs the field of customer complaints concerning Case New Holland of an initial no-start concern on QSX15 engines when the keyswitch is moved immediately from the “OFF” to “CRANK” position.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>This early field notification applies to all QSX15 engines used in both Case STX and New Holland TJ 4WD tractors.</p><p>The unit can come into the repair facility with a crank but no start concern.</p><p>Verify if the operator is <b>not</b> allowing sufficient time for the dash to be illuminated before attempting to crank the engine. The operator should be pausing for 2 to 3 seconds in the “RUN” position before trying to crank the engine.</p><p>Upon investigation, passing through the “RUN” position on the keyswitch to quickly will allow cranking before the ECM can command fueling. When this occurs the engine will crank, but will <b>not</b> start.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Make sure the operator of the unit is pausing for 2 to 3 seconds in the “RUN” position before trying to crank the engine in the event of a crank no start concern. The information in this bulletin is intended to inform the field how to educate the customer in the proper starting procedure of the engine, and to avoid any field service calls related to this complaint. Please distribute this bulletin to all industrial service managers, service writers, and field service technicians.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb070020":"<h2>Piston Skirt Scuffing</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Field Notification is to inform the field that QST30 and QSK23,45,60,78 engines with Ferrite Cast Iron Ductile (FCD) pistons are susceptible to piston skirt scuffing, at startup, after extended periods of shutdown during very cold ambient conditions. The field study data indicates that the engine is most vulnerable when starting with oil and coolant temperatures below −12°C [10°F].</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QST30, QSK23, QSK45, QSK60 and QSK78 engines</p><p>Some cases of high blow-by and coolant drop in the oil sump have been observed.</p><p>If an engine shows the symptoms of piston and liner scuffing, a center line inboard scuffing will be visible.</p><p>Scuffing occurs during cold starts, but may <b>not</b> exhibit any symptoms until more hours are accumulated.</p><p>The potential for piston, liner, connecting rod, crankshaft, and engine block damage exists.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>To reduce the potential for piston scuffing, it is recommended to warm the coolant and oil to a temperature of −4°C [25°F] prior to starting.</p><p>Cummins® distributors <b>must</b> work with their end user customers and/or OEM dealers to support this measure.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb070027":"<h2>Three-Piece Exhaust Manifolds - Unnecessary Repair</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Field Notification is to inform the field <b>not</b> to attempt repair of K19 and QSK19 three-piece exhaust manifolds that exhibit normal traces of carbon or carbon tracking near the slip joints.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><ul><li>QSK19 engines</li><li>K19 engines</li></ul><p>No engine performance concerns. Carbon tracking could possibly be present near the slip joints of the three-piece manifold.</p><p>None.</p><p>This is a normal characteristic for a three-piece manifold during the first 100 hours of operation. The carbon <b>must</b> form around the small clearances in the joints of the manifold in order for the joint to seal.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>None. If the <b>only</b> symptom is carbon tracking, no repair action is necessary.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb080038":"<h2>Cylinder Block and Centinel™ Valve Bracket</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification addresses an incompatibility issue between the present production cylinder block, Part Number 4965679 and Centinel™valve bracket, Part Number 3681176. The Centinel™valve bracket does <b>not</b> mount to the present cylinder block.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All QSX15 engines that use the Centinel™ fuel system and present production cylinder block.</p><p>The Centinel™ valve bracket will <b>not</b> mount to the cylinder block.</p><p>None.</p><p>There was an oversight at the release of the EGR product, due to the low volume usage of the Centinel™ fuel system.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01d00418.png\" alt=\"01d00418.png\"></figure><p>The Centinel™ valve bracket mounting hole, located on the bottom right, as viewed in the photo, will need to be slotted approximately 7.5 mm [0.295 in].</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb080053":"<h2>Non-Matching Connecting Rod and Rod Cap Serial Numbers</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification informs the field of a parts alert issued for the QSK45 and QSK60 straight split connecting rods Part Number 3640518. This requires all stock in the field to be checked to make sure the connecting rod and connecting rod cap serial numbers are the same.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>As of April 2008, this issue has been resolved at the supplier.</p></div></div><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All QSK45 and QSK60 connecting rods.</p><p>Non-matching connecting rod and connecting rod cap serial numbers have been found on new connecting rods being unpacked for assembly.</p><p>Connecting rod cap and connecting rod serial numbers should be identical. Connecting rod and connecting rod cap serial numbers can be found on the machined side of the big end of the connecting rod.</p><p>Quality of manufacturing process at supplier.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600476.png\" alt=\"01600476.png\"></figure><p>Any connecting rods found with non-matching serial numbers should <b>not</b> be used and returned to PDCs.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb080070":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Cooler Element Welds</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification informs the field that Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 lubricating oil cooler elements with the <b>supplier&#x27;s</b> weld marks are acceptable and can be used for repair in the field.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some lubricaing oil cooler elements do <b>not</b> have weld marks and are also acceptable.</p></div></div><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 engines are affected.</p><p>Observations will be the one or more weld marks from the supplier at any of the four corners of the lubricating oil cooler elements.</p><p>There is no failure. Lubricating oil cooler elements welded by the supplier are acceptable.</p><p>The standard manufacturing process at the supplier has a high fallout rate. Therefore, in order to meet the volume of demand, while making sure of product quality, some elements are being welded, tested, and supplied to Cummins Inc. for use in production and service. This process is controlled and approved by Cummins Inc. for this supplier <b>only</b>. Welding of lubricating oil cooler elements in the field is <b>not</b> acceptable.</p><p>This is not applicable.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Use lubricating oil cooler elements welded at the supplier for repairs in the field. Welding lubricating oil cooler elements in the field is <b>not</b> acceptable.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb080080":"<h2>Oil Cooler Cover Nut Gasket Leaks</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Some QSK45, QSK60, QSK78, and QSK60G engines are experiencing slow leaks at the oil cooler cover nut gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a>. For clarification, this gasket seals the large oil cooler studs. This is <b>not</b> the oil cooler plate gasket.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSK45, QSK60, QSK78, and QSK60G engines.</p><p>This issue can result in a slow external coolant leak.</p><p>There will be signs of engine coolant on top of the oil cooler cover around the large oil cooler nuts.</p><p>Still under investigation.</p><p>There is no potential for component damage.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Replace the paper gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a>, with an edge-molded gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3637730\">3637730</a>. Additionally, use Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375068, on the oil cooler stud threads.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb080089":"<h2>Alternator Issues in Arctic Conditions</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Delco-Remy™ 33SI alternators (Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3400698\">3400698</a>) are experiencing rear bearing failures in arctic conditions, where the ambient air temperature is less than -5°C [23°F].</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All K19 and QSK19 engines built with Delco-Remy™ 33SI alternators.</p><p>Customers are reporting that there is no charge to the battery, and on investigation, have found the rear bearing broken with progressive damage to the stator and rotor.</p><p>The alternator will <b>not</b> produce any charge when the engine is operating.</p><p>The grease and rear bearing used in the manufacture of the 33SI alternator is more susceptible to arctic weather conditions.</p><p>The rear bearing failure damages the alternator, resulting in replacement of the alternator with a new unit or an attempted field repair.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Replace failed Delco-Remy™ 33SI alternators with the Prestolite BLD 3314GH alternator, as the Prestolite alternator is more capable of coping with extreme arctic temperatures of -40°C [-40°F].</p><p>All 19L engines built after November 2008 for arctic applications now include the Prestolite BLD 3314GH alternator and the required change of pulleys, belt, and ground wire.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Alternator Options</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Delco-Remy™ 33SI</td><td>Prestolite BLD 3314GH</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Description</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>Delco-Remy™ 33SI Alternator</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3400698\">3400698</a></td><td>Prestolite BLD 3314GH Alternator</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3975140\">3975140</a></td></tr><tr><td>5-Groove Alternator Pulley</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3002323\">3002323</a></td><td>9-Groove Alternator Pulley</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4953300\">4953300</a></td></tr><tr><td>5-Groove Alternator Drive Pulley</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3002331\">3002331</a></td><td>9-Groove Alternator Drive Pulley</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4009258\">4009258</a></td></tr><tr><td>Cummins® 5-rib Belt</td><td>206996</td><td>Cummins® 9-rib Belt</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3024614\">3024614</a></td></tr><tr><td>Ground Wire</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3202162\">3202162</a></td><td>N/A</td><td>N/A</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>When upgrading to the Prestolite alternator, the ground wire will have to be changed as the Prestolite BLD 3314GH has a higher output than the Delco-Remy™ 33SI. The ground wire is presently <b>not</b> available for purchase from Cummins Inc.</p><p>There are no changes to the mounting bracket, tensioning arm, or the installation/removal and belt tension procedures, and no service tools required.</p><p>The specification for the ground wire is:</p><p>2 AWG</p><p>230 mm [9 in] long</p><p>One eyelet with an internal diameter of 6.35 mm [1/4 in]</p><p>One eyelet with an internal diameter of 9.53 mm [3/8 in]</p><p>This is shown in the photograph below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13400153.png\" alt=\"13400153.png\"></figure><p>Photographs of an installed Prestolite BLD 3314GH alternator.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13400154.png\" alt=\"13400154.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13400155.png\" alt=\"13400155.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13400156.png\" alt=\"13400156.png\"></figure><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090018":"<h2>INSITE™ 7.2 and PowerMatch™ Calibrations Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification describes an issue with INSITE™ 7.2 and PowerMatch™ calibrations. When attempting to transfer the PowerMatch™ calibration, INSITE™ 7.2 will show an error window and then close.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSB3.3 CM2150</p><p>QSB5.9 CM850</p><p>QSB4.5 CM850</p><p>QSB6.7 CM850</p><p>QSC8.3 CM554</p><p>QSC8.3 CM850</p><p>QSL9 CM554</p><p>QSL9 CM850</p><p>QSM11 CM570</p><p>QSX15 CM570</p><p>When trying to send a PowerMatch™ calibration with INSITE™ 7.2, an INSITE™ Service Diagnostic Program window will appear with Debug or Close options. An INSITE™ Service Diagnostic Program with Error Signature information and a Close button will appear. Clicking Close will close INSITE™ 7.2.</p><p>None</p><p>None</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Download INSITE™ 7.2 Service Pack 1 from INSITE™ website:</p><p>http://care.cummins.com</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb090024":"<h2>Air Leak Past Compressor Inlet Hose Coupling At Cylinder Head</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification informs the field that some ISX cylinder heads have a spot face at the compressor inlet hose coupling that is smaller than the fitting hex diameter and could possibly result in an air leak at the joint.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>Non EGR ISX family engines starting March 19, 2009 with engine serial number (ESN) First 79366820 and built with hose coupling, Part Number 3679303.</p><p>Symptoms include excessive compressor run time, compressed air system slow to build pressure, squealing, and other noise associated with air leaks at the compressor intake.</p><p>Confirm there is air leakage at the compressor inlet hose coupling due to interference between the coupling and the cast surface of the cylinder head.</p><p>The machined spot face is smaller than fitting diameter on some cylinder heads.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Modify the compressor inlet hose coupling to eliminate interference. Use a lathe to remove up to 3 mm [0.118 in] of material from the underside of the wrench flats to avoid interference and allow the coupling to seat in the machined spot face of the cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12c00172.png\" alt=\"12c00172.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1: Interference between coupling and cylinder head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12c00173.png\" alt=\"12c00173.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2: Interference corrected by modified coupling.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090029":"<h2>Injector Copper Seal Corrosion Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Field Notification is to inform the field that QSK45 and QSK60 series injector copper seals could possibly become corroded if high sulfur fuel (&gt;300 ppm) is used and either of the operating conditions listed below are present:</p><ol><li>Engine is operating more than 50 percent of the time at low idle (and load factor &lt;25 percent).</li><li>Ambient temperatures are below 5°C [41°F] for extended periods of time.</li></ol><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSK45 and QSK60 series engines with the HPI fuel system.</p><p>Sulfur corrosion has commonly been seen on QSK45 and QSK60 engines, but the potential exists for all QSK HPI engines to show signs of copper seal corrosion if the conditions listed above are met.</p><p>Copper seal corrosion is often referred to as a burned copper seal, due to the black marks found around the corroded or removed area.</p><p>Other symptoms could possibly include low cylinder temperatures or low power. Fault Code 621 (Exhaust Gas Temperature Deviation Low for Cylinder 1 - Data Valid But Below Normal Operational Range - Least Severe Level and Fault Code 622 (Exhaust Gas Temperature Deviation Low for Cylinder 3 - Data Valid But Below Normal Operational Range - Least Severe Level) have also been seen. Most failures, however, are seen at engine rebuild or during tear down for another failure.</p><p>Injector copper seal corrosion can be identified by noting that a portion of the copper seal appears to be dissolved or worn away.</p><p>Injector copper seals could possibly become corroded if high sulfur fuel (&gt;300 ppm) is used and either of the operating conditions listed below are present:</p><ol><li>Engine is operating more than 50 percent of the time at low idle (and load factor &lt;25 percent).</li><li>Ambient temperatures are below 5°C [41°F] for extended periods of time.</li></ol><ul><li>If the engine is operating within the boundaries suggested above, it is recommended that routine inspection of one or more injector seals be carried out at approximate 6 month intervals. Replacement of the fuel injector seal set is recommended if corrosion is found.</li></ul><p>Injector copper seal failures are normally seen at engine tear down due to another failure or during engine rebuild. The failure does <b>not</b> normally take the engine out of service, but it does increase the cost of the repair.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Replace corroded or burned copper seal with new seals (see figure 1). Analyze the sulfur content of fuel to make sure it is below 300 ppm. Analyze engine operation to make sure that the engine is not operating at low idle more than 50 percent (and load factor &lt;25 percent) of the time. If ambient conditions have been below 5°C [41°F] and fuel with a &gt;300 ppm sulfur content has been, used this could possibly also be an indication that copper seal damage is present. If repeated failures of copper seals are witnessed, it is recommended that the potential causes noted in this Early Field Notification be addressed for improved copper seal performance.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06600620.png\" alt=\"06600620.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1. Illustration of a burned copper seal.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090047":"<h2>Incorrectly Labeled Second Piston Rings</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The purpose of this Early Field Notification is to inform the field that second piston rings labeled with Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3090460\">3090460</a> could possibly be labeled incorrectly. The piston rings could possibly have been manufactured to the specifications of another piston ring.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>K19, K38, K50, QSK45, QSK45G, QSK60, and QSK60G</p><p>Any piston ring labeled with Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3090460\">3090460</a> (see Figure 1 in the Repair Instructions) could be labeled incorrectly. Part sets or kits which include this ring in them are Part Numbers 4025115, 4025116, 4089247, 4089500, 4924652, 4924653, 4955790, 4955910, 4955975, and 4956091.</p><p>Inspect the piston ring for a paint mark on the outer diameter. If it is marked with yellow paint, it was labeled correctly and can be used normally. If it is marked with blue paint, this ring has been mislabeled and can <b>not</b> be used (see Figures 2 and 3 in the Repair Instructions).</p><p>Piston ring, Part Number 3068813, was manufactured and labeled with Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3090460\">3090460</a> at the supplier, but painted with the correct identification color.</p><p>A study has been performed to confirm that the incorrect ring can <b>not</b> be installed into an engine. This is because the ring compressor will <b>not</b> fully close with the wrong ring installed. If an attempt is made to force the ring compressor to close; the ring groove on the piston could possibly be damaged.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Contact Customer Support and request a Return Goods Authorization (RGA) to return the piston ring set back to the Parts Distribution Center (PDC) from where it was purchased. If the piston ring set was purchased as part of an engine piston kit or overhaul kit, <b>only</b> return the piston ring set and keep the remaining parts in the kit.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400685.png\" alt=\"01400685.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Piston Ring Part Number</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400686.png\" alt=\"01400686.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, Correct Marking</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400687.png\" alt=\"01400687.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, Incorrectly Labeled Ring</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400688.png\" alt=\"01400688.png\"></figure><p>Figure 4, Piston Ring Set Packaging Label</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090055":"<h2>Calibration Bench Harness Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification describes an issue with the CM2150 calibration bench harness, Part Number 4918583. This cable presently uses the Cummins® Engine Network (CEN) for J1939 connections between a CM2150 electronic control module (ECM) and an electronic service tool (e.g. INSITE™) instead of the public J1939 network. Connections using CEN could possibly cause the ECM source address to be different than described in service manuals, specifically for engines with multi-module systems. Also, connection attempts made using this bench harness could possibly <b>only</b> succeed, if the attempt is made within a few seconds of key ON.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><ul><li>ISB CM2150</li><li>ISC CM2150</li><li>ISL CM2150</li><li>B3.9/5.9/C8.3 CM2150</li><li>ISDe CM2150C</li><li>ISLe CM2150</li><li>ISBe4 (4 and 6 cylinder) CM2150E</li><li>ISB4.5, 6.7 ISD4.5, 6.7 CM2150 SN (Euro 4.5)</li><li>ISB4.5, 6.7 ISD4.5, 6.7 CM2150 SN (Euro 5)</li><li>ISL8.9 CM2150 SN (Euro 4.5)</li><li>ISL8.9 CM2150 SN (Euro 5)</li><li>ISLe CM2150C</li><li>QSB3.3 CM2150</li><li>QSK19 CM2150 MCRS / Power Gen</li><li>QSK38 CM2150 MCRS / Power Gen</li><li>QSK50 CM2150 MCRS / Power Gen</li><li>QSK60 CM2150 MCRS / Power Gen</li></ul><p>The use of bench calibration harness, Part Number 4918583, with a WO number (listed at the bottom of the label on the cable), less than 190363, could possibly exhibit one of the following issues:</p><ol><li>An ECM that is calibrated will claim a different SAE J1939 source address as decribed in the service manuals. For example, a primary ECM from a multi-module system (switched to &quot;PRIM&quot; on the attached multiple module harness) normally claims SAE J1939 source address 00. On the CEN network with the same setup, the claimed SAE J1939 source address is 01 (which is the same for the secondary ECM on the public J1939 network).</li><li>An ECM that is calibrated and physically connected to an INLINE™ data link adapter, the CAN/J1939 light will <b>only</b> flash for a few seconds after a key ON. This light should remain flashing.</li></ol><p>One of the symptoms mentioned in the &quot;Symptoms and Observations&quot; section of this Early Field Notification and cable, Part Number 4918583, with a WO number less than 190363.</p><p>Bench calibration harness, Part Number 4918583, uses the CEN network for the J1939 connections.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Bench calibration harness, Part Number 4918583, has been rewired to use the public J1939 network. These new cables will have a WO number of 190363 or greater. Cables with WO number less than 190363 can be modified to use the public J1939 network.</p><p>To correct these cables, move terminal 51 to terminal location 01 and terminal 31 to terminal 21 on the OEM connector, using terminal removal tool, Part Number 3824815, or equivalent. The terminal removal procedure for Deutsch™ DRC connectors can be found in the following procedure in the appropriate Troubleshooting and Repair Manual. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/99-019-204\">Refer to Procedure 019-204 in Section 19.</a></p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090057":"<h2>Incorrect ECM Time (Key on time) in INSITE™ Fault Snapshot</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification describes an issue with INSITE™ 7.3 electronic service tool and earlier versions displaying the ECM Time (Key on time) in the fault snapshot data incorrectly when the Real Time Clock is enabled.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><ul><li>ISM CM876</li><li>ISB4.5/6.7 ISD4.5/6.7 CM2150 SN (Euro 4.5)</li><li>ISB4.5/6.7 ISD4.5/6.7 CM2150 SN (Euro 5)</li><li>QSK38 CM850 - MCRS</li><li>QSK50/60 CM850 - MCRS</li><li>QSM 11 CM876 - Power Generation</li><li>QSK38 CM850 -MCRS - Power Generation</li><li>QSK50/60 CM850 - MCRS - Power Generation</li></ul><p>The ECM Time (Key on time) is displayed incorrectly in the fault snapshot data in INSITE™ electronic service tool if the Real Time Clock is enabled in Advanced ECM Data. If the Real Time Clock is disabled, the ECM Time will be displayed correctly in the fault snapshot.</p><p>For example: if the Real Time Clock is enabled, the ECM Time is displayed incorrectly as 213274:47:16 (HH:MM:SS). If the Real Time Clock is disabled, the ECM Time is displayed correctly as 968:12:30 (HH:MM:SS).</p><p>None</p><p>None</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>This issue is fixed with INSITE™ 7.3 electronic service tool Service Pack 1 and later versions.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090062":"<h2>Oil Leak at Lower Front Cover</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification informs the field that a possible cause of an external oil leak from behind the vibration damper is a lower front gear cover manufacturing crack.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>ISX family engines starting with ESN 79372302, build date 08-May-09. This issue was corrected beginning 09-Jun-09 with ESN 79376451.</p><p>Symptoms and observations are an external oil leak that initiates behind the vibration damper and runs down the lower front gear cover.</p><p>Put dye in the oil and operate the engine to verify that the leak initiates from behind the vibration damper. Remove the vibration damper and inspect for a crack in the gear cover crankshaft seal boss at the 10 o&#x27;clock position. The typical crack location is at the bend transition between the flat cover surface and the raised stud boss.</p><p>Manufacturing issue at supplier resulting in a crack at this location.</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Replace the lower gear cover.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01c00803.png\" alt=\"01c00803.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01c00804.png\" alt=\"01c00804.png\"></figure><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090070":"<h2>Diesel Exhaust Fluid (DEF) Exhaust Blockage (Crystallization/Polymerization) and Fault Codes 1682, 2973, 2772, 2773, 3548, 3538, 3568, 3582, and 5655</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Product Affected</p><ul><li>All midrange engines equipped with aftertreatment selective catalyst reduction (SCR)</li></ul><p>Symptoms:</p><ul><li>Exhaust pipe diameters reduced by diesel exhaust fluid (DEF) crystallization or polymerization and/or DEF crystals visible externally.</li><li>Fault Codes 1682, 2973, 2772, 2773, 3548, 3538, 3568, 3582, and 5655.</li></ul><p>Root Cause:</p><ul><li>DEF crystals can build up in exhaust system for a number or reasons, including:</li><li>DEF crystals occur first and then turn into a polymer with prolonged temperature exposure below 290°C [ 554°F ].</li></ul><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>Crystallization or polymerization can lead to four types of exhaust piping blockage/restriction.</p><ol><li>Less than 20% DEF Accumulation (See Figure 1 below)</li><li>20 to 40 % DEF accumulation (See Figure 2 below)</li><li>40 to 50 % DEF Accumulation (See Figure 3 below)</li><li>50 to 80 % DEF Accumulation (See Figure 4 below)</li></ol><p><b>Additional Items</b></p><ul><li>External Buildup</li><li>Internal Decomposition Pipe Cleaning when crystallization leak is witnessed externally (DEF Injector Gasket). (See Figure 6 below).</li><li>DEF injector changes, Injectors seen to be “wet” or with a “drip” during system prime.</li><li>Duty Cycle and Exhaust System Design Considerations</li></ul><h3>Resolution</h3><ul><li>DEF accumulation covering less than 50% of cross sectional area does <b>not</b> need to be removed.</li><li>DEF accumulation above 50% <b>must</b> be removed. See corresponding Service Manual. Reference Procedure 011-062 in Section 11.</li><li>For any instances of reoccurring DEF accumulation where a resolution is <b>not</b> found using above information, a Technical Service Request (TSR) is to be raised.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00069.png\" alt=\"00u00069.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Less than 20% DEF Accumulation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00070.png\" alt=\"00u00070.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, 20% to 40% DEF Accumulation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00071.png\" alt=\"00u00071.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, 40% to 50% DEF Accumulation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00072.png\" alt=\"00u00072.png\"></figure><p>Figure 4, 50% to 80% DEF Accumulation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00073.png\" alt=\"00u00073.png\"></figure><p>Figure 5, External Buildup.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00u00074.png\" alt=\"00u00074.png\"></figure><p>Figure 6, Buildup of Fluid Noted from the DEF Injector Nozzle.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb090079":"<h2>Issue With Entering INSITE™ Electronic Service Tool Passwords on a Remote Desktop Connection</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification describes an issue with entering INSITE™ electronic service tool passwords on a remote desktop connection. It has been found that a remote desktop connection will prevent access to INSITE™ electronic service tool and passwords from being entered.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All engines supported by INSITE™ electronic service tool.</p><p>When attempting to open INSITE™ electronic service tool through a remote desktop connection, the program will prompt for a password to be entered. When trying to enter a password, an error message is given stating that, “The password entered is invalid”, even though the password has been verified.</p><p>N/A</p><p>N/A</p><p>N/A</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>This issue was corrected with INSITE™ electronic service tool 7.3 and later versions.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb090081":"<h2>External Oil Leak at Oil Pan</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Early Field Notification informs the field that a manufacturing issue could result in cracks and an external oil leak in the ISX oil pan.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>ISX Family Engines starting with ESN 79387906, build date 20-August-09. This issue was corrected beginning with ESN 79388492, build date 25-August-09.</p><p>Symptoms and observations are external oil leaks initiating at an oil pan crack. Crack locations can be along a weld, or along the ribbed area in the shallow end of the pan.</p><p>Visual inspection of an oil pan leak location.</p><p>A manufacturing issue at the supplier that resulted in oil pan cracks.</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Replace the oil pan.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100008":"<h2>Incorrect Torque Converter Orifice Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin addresses engines equipped with a torque converter that are experiencing high cooling system pressures, repeat coolant thermostat failures and/or cold cab conditions. For engines equipped with torque converters, an orifice is placed in the bypass hose from the water pump to the thermostat housing which diverts coolant flow to the torque converter. If the incorrect sized orifice is installed, the cooling system pressure can increase above acceptable levels, this can lead to coolant thermostat failures. Due to the high cooling system pressure the rubber on the coolant thermostat degrades, causing the thermostat <b>not</b> to seal correctly; this can lead to cold cab conditions.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to TRP or Campaign actions.</p></div></div><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>ISM, ISMe, QSM11, engines with a build date of January 1, 2007 and later that are equipped with a torque converter.</p><p>Symptoms and observations can include high cooling system pressures, repeat coolant thermostat failures, and cold cab conditions. It can also affect EGR cooler coolant flow.</p><p>None.</p><p>Incorrect orifice installed in the bypass hose between the water pump and the thermostat housing.</p><p>None.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Verify correct sized orifice for the engine.</p><p>Engines built with option TK2012 should have an orifice size of 22.22 mm [0.875 in]. This option is used on engines with EGR.</p><p>Engines built with option TK2008 should have an orifice size of 4.75 mm [0.187 in]. This option is used on engines without EGR.</p><p>Install correct orifice and replace any damaged components according to warranty guidelines.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100030":"<h2>Engine No Start Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin alerts the field to an issue with QST30 engines being built with the wrong relay in the engine lift pump harness. Engines were built with a 12 volt relay, Part Number 3658948, rather than the specified 24 volt relay, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3658780\">3658780</a>. This causes the 12 volt relay to become overloaded and fail. This prevents power from being supplied to the engine lift pumps and causes a no start condition at the next attempt to start the engine.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>This issue affects all QST30 engines. The suspected build range is estimated to be October 2009 to March 2010.</p><p>This issue is observed as a no start condition. The 12 volt relay becomes overloaded and typically fails within the first few running hours of a new engine. Depending on the fuel tank set up, the engine can remain running after the relay has malfunctioned. However, at the next attempt to start the engine, the no start condition will appear.</p><p>A 12 volt relay installed on the engine will show a lower resistance than the 24 volt relay across pins 85 and 86 on the lift pump harness connector. The resistance across pins 85 and 86 with the proper 24 volt relay installed will be in the range of 360-380 ohms. The resistance with the 12 volt relay installed will be approximately 75 ohms.</p><p>The supplier of the lift pump wiring harness installed the incorrect relay in the harness.</p><p>Overheated relay. No progressive damage is expected.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>If a 12 volt relay is found damaged, or a low resistance is found across pins 85 and 86 of the lift pump harness, replace the relay with the 24 volt relay, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3658780\">3658780</a>.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100033":"<h2>Coolant Level Sensor Leakage Issues</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin describes a condition in which the coolant level sensor can malfunction, allowing coolant to seep into the wiring harness and into other sensors and electronic control system devices. Both two wire and three wire coolant level sensors have been observed to leak internally. 2007 and 2010 EPA-certified automotive engines built with an aftertreatment system can experience white smoke in extreme cases where coolant seeps through the wiring harness to the aftertreatment diesel particulate filter differential pressure sensor.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>Automotive, Industrial, and Marine applications are affected.</p><ul><li>ISB CM2250</li></ul><ul><li>ISB CM2150</li></ul><ul><li>ISB CM850</li></ul><ul><li>QSB CM850</li></ul><ul><li>ISC CM2250</li></ul><ul><li>ISC CM2150</li></ul><ul><li>ISC CM850</li></ul><ul><li>QSC CM850</li></ul><ul><li>ISL CM2250</li></ul><ul><li>ISL CM2150</li></ul><ul><li>ISL CM850</li></ul><ul><li>QSL CM850</li></ul><ul><li>ISM CM876</li></ul><ul><li>ISM CM875</li></ul><ul><li>QSM CM570</li></ul><ul><li>ISX CM2250</li></ul><ul><li>ISX CM871</li></ul><ul><li>ISX CM870</li></ul><ul><li>QSX CM570</li></ul><p>Symptoms can vary by engine family, OEM, and application. Symptoms include, but are <b>not</b> limited to:</p><ul><li>Slow coolant consumption.</li><li>Coolant level sensor fault codes. The engine ECM does <b>not</b> always log a fault code for the coolant level sensor when it begins to leak coolant internally.</li><li>Electronic system component corrosion.</li><li>Electronic system component electrical connections wet with coolant.</li><li>White smoke. This <b>only</b> occurs on engines built with an aftertreatment system and an aftertreatment diesel particulate filter differential pressure sensor.</li></ul><p>Disconnect the wiring harness from the coolant level sensor and inspect the male and female connections for evidence of coolant intrusion. The electrical connection is a tight seal and an external leak will <b>not</b> be evident. The same should also be done to the aftertreatment sensor connectors.</p><p>The coolant level sensor is leaking internally. Current coolant level sensors are manufactured with materials that can <b>not</b> withstand exposure to extended life coolant.</p><p>Extended operation with a leaking coolant level sensor will result in total contamination of the engine wiring harness. It will be necessary to disconnect the harness connectors, including the OEM 60-pin ECM connector, to inspect for coolant intrusion. Replace any damaged components.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Coolant level sensors are commonly OEM-supplied. Depending upon vehicle application, it is possible that the sensor was supplied by Cummins Inc. The simplest method to determine who supplied the sensor, is to view the part number stamped on the sensor and determine if that part number is a Cummins part number or an OEM part number. If the sensor is OEM-supplied, work with the vehicle OEM to replace any damaged harnesses, sensors, ECMs, or other control modules that are part of the electronic control system. This is <b>not</b> a failure warrantable by Cummins® Inc. Repair locations should work with the vehicle OEM for warranty reimbursement.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19804021.png\" alt=\"19804021.png\"></figure><p>Coolant intrusion in the coolant sensor.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19804022.png\" alt=\"19804022.png\"></figure><p>A corroded electrical connection that requires replacement.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100044":"<h2>Air Compressor Support Brackets Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>The air compressor support brackets (Option CP4073 or CP4076) on QSK19 and K19 engines equipped with twin cylinder air compressor (Part Number 3103409) have been wearing or cracking/breaking. This can result in loss of support for the air compressor and lead to compressor damage. It is recommended that the brackets be checked for wear or cracks at the next regularly scheduled 250 hour maintenance interval.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>This issue affects all QSK19 and K19 engines built or upfit with a twin cylinder air compressor, option CP4073 or CP4076. The brackets that have been cracking or showing signs of wear are Part Numbers 4081295 and 4081296.</p><p>The issue is noted by wear or fretting between the sleeve and the holes in the brackets. This wear can cause the joint to become loose.</p><p>Cracking/breaking of the welds has also been observed.</p><p>To verify the malfunction, check the brackets and sleeve for wear. Check the sleeve for grooves or wear marks. Also, check the holes in the bracket for wear or deformation.</p><p>Check the welds on the bracket for cracking or other signs of damage.</p><p>If any of this is observed, the bracket assembly <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>The cause is suspected to be excessive movement in the bracketry during engine operation. Movement in the bracket causes wear in the sleeve and bracket holes. This wear allows for increased vibration and oscillating load on the bracket and compressor housing.</p><p>Bracket cracking/breaking or wear can cause progressive damage to the compressor housing, as seen below. Compressor housings have been found cracked or broken due to lack of support from a worn or broken bracket.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Inspect the brackets at the regularly scheduled 250 hour maintenance intervals or during other repairs. If cracking/breaking or wear is seen, the brackets <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12400054.png\" alt=\"12400054.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12400055.png\" alt=\"12400055.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12400056.png\" alt=\"12400056.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/12400057.png\" alt=\"12400057.png\"></figure><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100048":"<h2>INSITE™ Electronic Service Tool 7.4 - Windows® 7 - Internet Explorer® 8 - Fault Information System Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin describes an issue with INSITE™ electronic service tool version 7.4 (7.4.0.244), on Windows® 7, with Internet Explorer® 8, when opening the fault information system (FIS). After opening a fault code, a script error window will open, instead of the troubleshooting steps.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All engines supported with INSITE™ electronic service tool.</p><p>When opening the troubleshooting steps for a Fault Code with INSITE™ electronic service tool, a Script Error window will open.</p><p>None</p><p>The older FIS files format includes a pop-up warning window.</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Click Yes or No on the Script Error window to open the Fault Code troubleshooting steps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19000001.png\" alt=\"19000001.png\"></figure><p>Screenshot of error message in INSITE™ Update Manager</p><p>The FIS files are being reformatted and will have this warning window removed. Periodically check the Cummins INSITE™ Update Manager for updated FIS files.</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100049":"<h2>Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Leaks</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>There have been a number of front and rear crankshaft seal leaks on QSK45/60/78 engines in production test. The cause of the leak has been determined to be a manufacturing issue with the seal. The affected seals are from specific batch numbers. These numbers have been identified and are shown below. All seals with the batch numbers shown below <b>must</b> be removed from parts distribution centers (PDC) and distributor stock in order to prevent repeat malfunctions in the field. This issue was found during production testing and few, if any, seals were installed on production engines.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>QSK45 CM500</p><p>QSK60 CM500, CM850, CM2150</p><p>QSK78 CM500</p><p>If a seal from one of the batches has been used on an engine, it may result in a low hour oil leak from the seal. <b>Only</b> seals that match the date codes below should be removed from stock.</p><p>If it is suspected that a crankshaft seal matching these batch numbers has been installed on an engine it is recommended that the engine&#x27;s oil level is monitored closely.</p><p>Crankshaft seals that match the part number and the batch numbers shown below should be removed from stock and <b>not</b> used on any engine.</p><h4>Front crankshaft Seal Batch Numbers (Part Number: 4100624)</h4><ul><li>09-131</li><li>09-280</li><li>09-323</li></ul><h4>Rear crankshaft Seal Batch Numbers (Part Number: 4100625)</h4><ul><li>09-196</li><li>09-133</li></ul><p>The suspected cause of the seal leaks is a supplier quality issue, which has been corrected.</p><p>There is no progressive damage to the engine if a seal from one of the mentioned batch numbers is installed. However, it could result in extensive down time while the seal is changed.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>All stock of crankshaft seals <b>must</b> be checked against the batch numbers listed. If any seals match the batch numbers they <b>must</b> be removed from stock and <b>not</b> used.</p><p>Return the seals that match the batch numbers to PDC where they were purchased, referencing the Parts Alert Number 012-10.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600680.png\" alt=\"01600680.png\"></figure><p>Location of Part Number and Batch Number on the Seal</p><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100051":"<h2>INSITE™ 7.4 Features and Parameters Display Issue</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin describes an issue with INSITE™ electronic service tool version 7.4 (7.4.0.244) displaying the Features and Parameters column incorrectly (too narrow). This causes the rows to widen and makes it difficult to read the feature names.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>All Engines supported by INSITE™ electronic service tool.</p><p>Open Features and Parameters while connected to an ECM and the first column is narrow and the rows are wide.</p><p>None</p><p>INSITE™ electronic service tool version 7.4 (7.4.0.244) is automatically adjusting the first column width incorrectly on some screen resolutions.</p><p>None</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>Manually adjust the width of the first column:</p><ul><li>Move the curser over the column line until it changes to a double arrow.</li><li>While holding the left mouse button down, move the column line to the right until the column width has increased and then release the mouse button.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000028.png\" alt=\"22000028.png\"></figure><p>After resizing the column, the row width will automatically adjust.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22000029.png\" alt=\"22000029.png\"></figure><p>Change the display resolution to any of the following settings:</p><ul><li>800 by 600</li><li>1024 by 768</li><li>1280 by Any</li><li>1152 by 864</li></ul><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p>","tsb100075":"<h2>C Cylinder Head Capscrew - Torque Plus Angle</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin has been superseded by Service/Parts Topic 99T2-6.</p>","tsb100077":"<h2>Cylinder Head Torque For New Block and Capscrews</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin has been superseded by Service/Parts Topic 99T2-6.</p>","tsb100081":"<h2>Oil Volumes for Isolated Oil Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>Certain options and kits require the addition of extra oil when performing an oil change. Both the isolation oil pan gasket option and the bedplate (block stiffener) option each require additional oil to be added during the oil change. The dipstick tube does <b>not</b> need to be changed.</p><p>Engines with the following part numbers for the isolation gasket or the bedplate <b>must</b> add extra oil.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, 4B Series Engine (liters/quarts of oil needed)</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Oil Pan Part No.</td><td>Normal Level</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3929093</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3929093, and Gasket, Part No. 3932138</td></tr><tr><td>3901049</td><td>9.5 liters [10 qt]</td><td>12 liters [12.5 qt]</td><td>14.5 liters [15.5 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3907570</td><td>9.5 liters [10 qt]</td><td>12 liters [12.5 qt]</td><td>14.5 liters [15.5 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3917918</td><td>9.5 liters [10 qt]</td><td>12 liters [12.5 qt]</td><td>14.5 liters [15.5 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3924151</td><td>9.5 liters [10 qt]</td><td>12 liters [12.5 qt]</td><td>14.5 liters [15.5 qt]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, 6B Series Engine (liters/quarts of oil needed)</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Oil Pan Part No.</td><td>Normal Level</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3941556</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3941556, and Gasket, Part No. 3931996</td></tr><tr><td>3915073</td><td>14 liters [15 qt]</td><td>17 liters [18 qt]</td><td>21 liters [22 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3924489</td><td>16 liters [17 qt]</td><td>18 liters [19 qt]</td><td>23 liters [24 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3925772</td><td>9.5 liters [10 qt]</td><td>12 liters [13 qt]</td><td>15 liters [16 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3924152</td><td>14 liters [15 qt]</td><td>17 liters [18 qt]</td><td>20 liters [21.5 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3916614</td><td>10 liters [11 qt]</td><td>13 liters [14 qt]</td><td>16 liters [17 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3924153</td><td>14 liters [15 qt]</td><td>17 liters [17.5 qt]</td><td>19 liters [20 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3914403</td><td>10 liters [11 qt]</td><td>13 liters [14 qt]</td><td>16 liters [17 qt]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, 6C Series Engine (liters/quarts of oil needed)</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Oil Pan Part No.</td><td>Normal Level</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3927606</td><td>Level with Bedplate, Part No. 3927606, and Gasket, Part No. 3931967</td></tr><tr><td>3914013 (front sump)</td><td>19 liters [20 qt]</td><td>22 liters [23 qt]</td><td>25 liters [26.5 qt]</td></tr><tr><td>3914015 (center)</td><td>19 liters [20 qt]</td><td>22 liters [23 qt]</td><td>26 liters [27 qt]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07900190.png\" alt=\"07900190.png\"></figure><p>Isolation Gasket</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00900098.png\" alt=\"00900098.png\"></figure><p>Bedplate</p>","tsb100092":"<h2>Wet Flywheel Housing Crankshaft Oil Seal</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces a wet flywheel housing crankshaft oil seal, Part Number 3681527 (see Fig. 1). Use the thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal installation and removal kit, Part Number 3163826, to install and remove the wet flywheel housing crankshaft oil seal. Both the new oil seal and kit are for use on Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Series engines in applications with wet flywheel housings.</p><p>The thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal installation and removal kit <b>must</b> be used to install the new rear crankshaft oil seal and thick wear sleeve.</p><p>The thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal installation and removal kit includes the thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal installation and removal procedure (Bulletin 3377856).</p><p>The wet flywheel housing crankshaft oil seal and wear sleeve is one assembly. It <b>must not</b> be taken apart. <b>No</b> oil is to be used during the installation procedure.</p><p>If the crankshaft flange is scored, repair the surface. Refer to Alternative Repair Manual, Bulletin 3379035.</p><p><b>Release Date</b></p><p>The wet flywheel housing crankshaft oil seal, Part Number 3681527, and the thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal installation and removal kit, Part Number 3163826, both became available in January 2000.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01c00322.png\" alt=\"01c00322.png\"></figure><p>Fig. 1, Wet Flywheel Housing Crankshaft Oil Seal</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00158.png\" alt=\"22c00158.png\"></figure><p><b>Table 1, Thick Wear Sleeve and Wet Flywheel Housing Oil Seal Installation and Removal Kit, Part Number 3163826</b></p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item Number</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3163827</td><td>Thick wear sleeve and wet flywheel housing oil seal mandrel</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163706</td><td>Puller jaws</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>S-217</td><td>Hexagon nut (7/16-14)</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3000082\">3000082</a></td><td>Flat washer (7/16 x 7/8)</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3163057</td><td>Forcing screw</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3163828</td><td>Number 10-2 sheet metal screw</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>3163089</td><td>Pilot drill</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not</b> shown</td><td>3377856</td><td>Service Tool Instruction</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb100105":"<h2>Flexible Fuel Line</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin introduces a new flexible steel-braided fuel line (1) for the M11 and ISM/QSM11 Series engines. This flexible fuel line supersedes the hard steel line that supplies fuel from the fuel pump to the ECM cooling plate. (See Fig. 1.)</p><p>This flexible fuel line was implemented into production with engine serial number first 35009935 on June 19, 2000.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Old and New Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Description</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>Hard steel fuel line</td><td>3161626</td><td>N/A</td></tr><tr><td>Flexible fuel line</td><td>N/A</td><td>4060562</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13200093.png\" alt=\"13200093.png\"></figure><p>Fig. 1, Flexible Steel-Braided Fuel Line</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>"};
